    "content": "# carrier_definition.md — substantive source view v0.2\n\nOriginal intake object: A12. Original bytes are preserved.\nPresentation class: SOURCE-LINKED RECONSTRUCTION. Physical promotion: 0. This page is newly authored from named sources; it is not the recovered historical original.\n\n## Carrier definition with typed distinctions\n\nThe filled tetrahedron has 15 real graded chain coefficients. S4 times its eight-state matching fiber is a 192-element labeled binary state set. A prepared apparatus Hilbert space, boundary memory register and four-amplitude metric block are different objects. Domains and codomains, metric/normalization, orientation and readout must be supplied before mapping them. Equal dimensions or equal numbers do not identify carriers.\n\n## Source-bound ledger entries\n\n- LEDGER:P05 N1 = 24 * 8 = 192 [EXACT_INTERNAL]. Scope: ACTIVE / SECTION-7 DEPENDENCY. Next gate: any observable interpretation must be derived separately\n- LEDGER:Q51 N_active^chain = 14 [EXACT_INTERNAL]. Scope: AUTO_LOCK / NOT SPACETIME DIMENSION. Next gate: none for count; physical interpretation separately gated\n- LEDGER:Q165 S_mu^rev = \\|\\|c0\\|\\|^2+\\|\\|c1\\|\\|^2+\\|\\|c2\\|\\|^2+\\|\\|c3\\|\\|^2 [LOCKED_INTERNAL_MATHEMATICS]. Scope: AUTO_LOCK / admitted micro support carrier. Next gate: global gluing/coarse recursive support bridge\n- LEDGER:Q169 A_K^global = global skew Hodge-Dirac on unique C0⊕C1⊕C2⊕C3 simplices [LOCKED_MATHEMATICAL_GEOMETRY]. Scope: AUTO_LOCK. Next gate: open-system support terms\n- LEDGER:Q180 PSR(c) = ({rho_sigma},{chi_sigma,tau}_F,{epsilon_C}) [LOCKED_INTERNAL_MATHEMATICS]. Scope: AUTO_LOCK / SUFFICIENT PROJECTIVE SUPPORT RECEIPT ON NONZERO CHAIN STATE. Next gate: same-carrier acquisition of the required stock/current/root-sign receipt\n\n## Exact source and version crosswalk\n\n- PI: Finite Tetrahedral Complexes, Skew Support Flow and Contact Readiness — https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/47121c4b2d8f472c4eaa977b475d20cc267eed