    "content": "# Artifact Dependency Map\n\n## Purpose\nThis file replaces the placeholder with a populated dependency summary for the current Distinction / Packet Dynamics program.\n\n## 1. Governance root\nAll major artifacts depend first on the canonical repository alignment sequence. No downstream artifact is considered stable unless governance alignment is complete.\n\n## 2. Core dependency spine\nThe current dependency spine is:\n\n1. primitive substrate definitions,\n2. trion admissibility rule,\n3. residue definition,\n4. minimal volumetric closure (tetrahedral packet),\n5. compression/regeneration hierarchy,\n6. coherence-retention law,\n7. transport/seam operators,\n8. curvature and burden/depth bridge,\n9. matter/gauge emergence,\n10. cosmology and packet-dynamics simulation,\n11. replication and complexity,\n12. knowledge layer.\n\n## 3. Key artifact relationships\n### Primitive substrate\nDepends on:\n- simplicial complex \\(K\\),\n- binary distinction field \\(b\\in C^0(K,\\mathbb{Z}_2)\\),\n- trion admissibility.\n\nFeeds:\n- residue theory,\n- tetrahedral closure,\n- simulation initialization.\n\n### Coherence equation\nDepends on:\n- tetrahedral packet architecture,\n- information budget count \\(I_{\\text{eff}}=31\\),\n- reconstruction anchoring regime.\n\nFeeds:\n- spectral index bridge,\n- cosmological observables program,\n- evidence comparison.\n\n### Seam transport\nDepends on:\n- face orientation,\n- framing variables \\(\\sigma\\),\n- branch variables \\(\\chi\\),\n- phase variables \\(\\theta\\).\n\nFeeds:\n- gauge emergence,\n- defect propagation,\n- curvature-from-holonomy analysis.\n\n### Dirac-like defect equation\nDepends on:\n- seam transport,\n- framing topology,\n- emergent gauge couplings.\n\nFeeds:\n- fermionic matter sector,\n- low-energy effective action.\n\n### Master action\nDepends on:\n- burden/depth gravity bridge,\n- gauge transport sectors,\n- defect sectors,\n- closure-background order parameter.\n\nFeeds:\n- continuum phenomenology,\n- funding-grade theory presentation,\n- later test linkage.\n\n### Packet dynamics\nDepends on:\n- packet state variables \\((\\rho,\\theta,\\chi)\\),\n- nonlinear update rules,\n- routing memory,\n- environment coupling.\n\nFeeds:\n- replication,\n- ecosystem stability,\n- knowledge emergence.\n\n## 4. Current dependency priority\nThe currently favored development order remains:\n\n1. formal core definitions,\n2. local toy model,\n3. derive \\(\\eta\\),\n4. metric program,\n5. gauge/quantum precursors,\n6. matter sector.\n\n## 5. Risk concentration\nCurrent high-dependency, high-risk nodes are:\n\n- the coarse-graining bridge from packet microdynamics to continuum geometry,\n- quantitative branch-weight derivation,\n- full carrier formalization,\n- explicit Standard-Model-level matching,\n- empirical simulation-to-observable calibration.\n"
