    "content": "# Text access to the original historical document\n\nStatus: historical proposal; equations and layout should be checked in the original download. Text extraction is an access aid, not a new derivation.\n\nRecursive General Relativity as a Class-Conditioned Response Theory\nBenjamin Mayes\nAbstract\nWe propose a contained reformulation of General Relativity in which Einstein gravity is recovered as the smooth fixed-class limit of a broader recursive response structure. The formalism is organized in two layers: a discrete class structure specifying admissibility, regime identity, support organization, and protection status, followed by a continuous logarithmic response law governing observables within the selected class. Within this framework, the standard geometric description of gravitation is preserved as the leading low-burden regime, while strong-regime seams are interpreted either as steep in-class response or as genuine class transitions. This yields a compact language for source dressing, threshold behavior, and regime-dependent observables without relying on additive patch terms.\n1. Introduction\nGeneral Relativity remains the most successful classical theory of gravitation. Its significance is not exhausted by the familiar statement that gravity has been geometrized. More deeply, the theory reorganizes the relation between gravitation, inertia, and motion into a unified geometric description. In the regime where spacetime response is smooth and the relevant support structure remains fixed, that description is both conceptually powerful and empirically indispensable.\nThe purpose of this companion document is to provide a formatting-stable prose-aligned version of the Recursive GR manuscript suitable for\n \n.docx\n \npackaging and sharing. It follows the same contained posture as the LaTeX manuscript and preserves the main formal definitions and equations in a lightweight submission-friendly layout.\n2. Core Formal Definitions\nThe native accommodation coordinates are:\nx\n=\nθ\n,\na\n,\nc\n,\nb\nThe discrete class state is:\nK\n=\nA\n,\nχ\n,\nP\n,\nN\n,\nC\n,\nS\nThe logarithmic response field is:\nΔ\nQ\n|\nK\nx\n=\nln\nQ\nK\nQ\nK\n,\n0\nThe master class-conditioned response law is:\nQ\nK\n=\nQ\nK\n,\n0\nexp\nΔ\nQ\n|\nK\nx\nThe threshold gap is:\nΓ\nX\n|\nK\n=\nln\nX\nK\nX\nc\nr\ni\nt\n,\nK\nThe selector gap is:\nΣ\nα\nβ\n|\nK\n=\nln\nΠ\nα\n|\nK\nΠ\nβ\n|\nK\n3. Einstein Recovery\nRecursive General Relativity does not begin by displacing Einstein gravity. Its first task is to clarify the formal status of Einstein gravity’s success. The effective source law is written as:\nT\nμ\nν\n|\nK\ne\nf\nf\n=\nT\nμ\nν\n|\nK\nG\nR\nexp\nΔ\nT\nμ\nν\n|\nK\nThe class-conditioned field equation is:\nG\nμ\nν\n|\nK\n=\n8\nπ\nT\nμ\nν\n|\nK\ne\nf\nf\nIn the fixed-class weak-dressing limit, one recovers Einstein gravity:\nG\nμ\nν\n|\nK\nG\nR\n=\n8\nπ\nT\nμ\nν\n|\nK\nG\nR\nG\nR\n4. Contained Bridge to Local Field Description\nA useful contained interpretation is to treat spacetime as the effective large-scale geometry of an organized oscillatory transport field rather than as a passive background. At coarse scale one may summarize this organization by:\nΨ\nx\n,\nt\n=\nρ\nx\n,\nt\ne\ni\nϕ\nx\n,\nt\nIn this reading, time corresponds to coherent phase advance, space to effective transport adjacency, curvature to nonuniformity in the organization of the field, and matter to persistent defect structure within the same fabric. This is used here only as a controlled interpretive bridge between smooth geometry and local sector description.\n5. Canonical Exemplar\nThe seam/framing sector provides the first closed exemplar of the architecture. The onset of breaking is written as a genuine class transition:\nK\np\nr\ne\n→\nK\nb\nr\no\nk\ne\nn\nWithin the broken neutral class, the protected mode obeys:\nm\nA\n=\n0\nThe burdened neutral and charged modes obey:\nm\nZ\n=\nm\nZ\n,\n0\nexp\nΔ\nm\nZ\n|\nK\nZ\nm\nW\n=\nm\nW\n,\n0\nexp\nΔ\nm\nW\n|\nK\nW\nThe neutral mixing angle is governed by:\nΘ\nm\ni\nx\n=\narctan\ng\n1\n,\n0\ng\n2\n,\n0\nexp\nΔ\ng\n1\n|\nK\nZ\n−\nΔ\ng\n2\n|\nK\nZ\n6. Conclusion\nRecursive General Relativity is a contained class-conditioned response theory in which Einstein gravity is recovered as the fixed-class smooth limit, while gravitational seams are interpreted either as steep in-class response, support reorganization, or genuine class transition. The\n \n.docx\n \ncompanion preserves the main formal spine of the manuscript while keeping the deeper exploratory program outside the submission burden."
