    "content": "# Text access to the original historical document\n\nStatus: historical proposal; equations and layout should be checked in the original download. Text extraction is an access aid, not a new derivation.\n\nUnified Dynamics (Distinction Theory) v2.2: Master Manuscript\n\n1. Front Matter and Abstract\nTitle: Unified Dynamics: A Typed, Weighted Operator Grammar for Geometry and\nMatterAuthors: Benjamin Walker Mayes, et al.Status: Final — Canonical Artifact Stack (v2.2)\n\nAbstract\nThis manuscript formalizes Unified Dynamics (UD) v2.2, a non-perturbative framework modeling\nphysical reality as a typed, weighted operator grammar for geometry and matter. By defining a\nrecursive architecture of distinction and closure on a simplicial substrate, we achieve a\nsynthesis of the 28-prediction scorecard (14 exact, 6 confirmed, 8 candidates). We report the\nresolution of the cosmological constant gap and the \"Null\" computational field via the F6 $N=7$\nsimulation. Results indicate that the injection of simplicial gravity (Einstein coupling $\\kappa =\n1/9\\pi^2$ ) provides the requisite geometric attraction via curvature defects ( $\\epsilon = \\pi$ ),\ncreating a potential well that clamps previously monotone computational fields into stable matter\npackets.\n\nCompanion Header\nFeature,Geometry Companion (Relaxed Coarse Isotropic Limit),Matter Companion (Minimal\nTwo-Primitive Operator Set)\nPrimary Claim,General Relativity emerges as the coarse isotropic relaxed limit of the substrate\nresponse.,\"Particle families are generated by a minimal set of two primitive operator blocks (\n$S_0, H$ ).\"\nFormalism,\"$G_{\\mu\\nu} = \\kappaT^{(GR)} + \\Delta T^{(\\theta, a, c, b)}$\",$Q_{obs} = Q_0(1 +\nz_Q)$\nLogic,Substrate response to burdened states (curvature as transport mismatch).,State grammar\ndefining stable burdened states (matter as persistent defect structure).\nKey Equation,Corrected Einstein Block with four accommodation channels.,\"Seed-and-Lift\nladder ( $e, \\mu, \\tau$ mass operators).\"\n\n2. Part I: Ontological Grammar and Primitive Substrate\n\nThe Core Grammar: Simplicial Evolution\nThe transition from a primary distinction to recursive complexity follows a rigorous nine-stage\nhierarchy of operator flow:\n  1.​ Point (Primitive Locus): The foundational possibility of identity; the initial locus of\n       distinction.\n  2.​ Line (First Distinction): Binary linkage of two points; the act of non-closure\n       differentiation.\n  3.​ Triangle (First Coherent Relation): The minimal closed loop; the birth of structural\n       coherence.\n\f 4.​   Hexagon (Surround Path): Operator flow bifurcation into the \"Surround\" channel (\n       $C_2$ wrapping); planar completion.\n 5.​   Pyramid (Lift Gesture): Flow bifurcation into the \"Lift\" channel ( $\\partial$ boundary\n       extension); dimensional escape.\n 6.​   Tetrahedron (First Locked Lock): Completion of the lift; the first stable 3D volumetric\n       primitive.\n 7.​   Octahedron (First Balanced Compound): Resolution of polarity; two pyramids joined\n       at the base.\n 8.​   Icosahedron (First Global Shell): Efficient 3D spherical enclosure; 20 triangular faces.\n 9.​   600-Cell (Recursion): 4D recursive shell; the previous shell becomes the building block\n       for the next iteration.\n\nSubstrate Primitives\nThe substrate comprises Locations and Transport Links . The node state is formalized as\nthe triplet $\\Psi = (\\rho, \\theta, \\chi)$ , where $\\rho$ denotes burden (unresolved load),\n$\\theta$ denotes local orientation, and $\\chi$ denotes the specific closure branch.\n\nBinary-Ternary Unification\nThe substrate is fundamentally ternary, defined by 3 axes with 3 states ( $+1, 0, -1$ ), yielding\n$3^3 = 27$ configurations.\n   ●​ Particle-Aspect (Binary): Closure-entities require discrete identity. The\n       \"neither/between\" zero-states are filtered, leaving $2^3 = 8$ binary configurations for\n       observation.\n   ●​ Field-Content: The 19 configurations involving at least one zero-state ( $27 - 8 = 19$ )\n       constitute the \"field content\" present across the substrate.\n   ●​ Deficit: The binary deficit $\\Delta=7$ governs particle-regime interactions, while the\n       full ternary deficit (26) governs cosmological scaling.\n\n3. Part II: The Retained Existence Engine (REE)\n\nAxioms of Retained Existence\n   ●​ X.1 Distinction: Legibility emerges only at the appearance of a distinction.\n   ●​ X.2 Local Binary Retention: Every distinction induces a local keep/release event\n      $\\{0,1\\}$ .\n   ●​ X.3 Recursive Accumulation: Retained distinctions integrate recursively across the\n      graph.\n   ●​ X.4 Mechanical Formation Floor: Minimum viability requires closure, transport, and\n      burden tolerance.\n   ●​ X.5 Triadic Existence Agreement: Consensus between Omega logic ( $\\Omega$ ),\n      Admissibility (Adm), and Support (Supp).\n   ●​ X.6 Closure: Stability is contingent upon locked, non-loose-ended state configurations.\n   ●​ X.7 Temporal Retention: Momentary closure must persist through time to manifest as\n      \"world.\"\n\f    ●​ X.8 Stratified Selection: Selection is governed by authority layers (Formation $\\to$\n       Retention $\\to$ Strain $\\to$ Propagation).\n    ●​ X.9 Selector Asymmetry: Foundational gate collapse is terminal; secondary failure\n       induces adaptive strain.\n    ●​ X.10 Existence Update: Structure is continually reselected via the Update Engine (\n       $U$ ).\n\nThe Construction Spine\nThe ontological progression is formalized via the Construction Spine: Distinction $\\to$\nBinary retention $\\to$ Recursive accumulation $\\to$ Triadic agreement $\\to$ Closure\n$\\to$ Temporal retention $\\to$ World.\n\nPrecedence Resolution Order\nWhen overlapping conditions exist, the Update Engine ( $U$ ) resolves states according to the\nfollowing hierarchy:| Precedence Order | Resulting Outcome | Description || ------ | ------ | ------ ||\n1. Dissolve | Highest Authority | Total structural erasure. || 2. Expel | Terminal | Removal from\nthe world-graph. || 3. Fragment | Terminal | Dissolution of coherent identity. || 4. Repair |\nAdaptive | Restoration via drift sensitivity. || 5. Strained | Adaptive | Survival under secondary\ngate failure. || 6. Propagate | Extension | Expansion of coherent structure. || 7. Stable |\nGround State | Maintenance of the current state. |\n\n4. Part III: Universal Structure Theorem and Simplicial Variation\n\nSimplicial Boundary Channels\nThe $K_4$ (Tetrahedron) structure supports independent variation channels through its graded\nsimplex boundary operator ( $\\partial$ ) and co-boundary ( $\\delta$ ):\n   ●​ $\\delta^0$ (Vertices $\\to$ Edges): Maps to Frame Variation .\n   ●​ $\\delta^1$ (Edges $\\to$ Faces): Maps to Connection Variation .\n   ●​ $\\delta^2$ (Faces $\\to$ Body): Maps to Curvature Integration .\n\n4 $\\pi$ Angular Normalization Lemma\nThe dimensionless coupling $\\alpha_{body} = 1/\\pi^2$ is derived by normalizing the $K_4$\ncoupling against the full angular support of the local 3D orientation field:\n  1.​ Let $g_{body}^2 = 4/\\pi$ (derived from the Regge curvature quantum $\\epsilon = \\pi$ ).\n  2.​ Define $\\Omega = 4\\pi$ as the complete angular support of a unit sphere in 3D.\n  3.​ The dimensionless coupling is obtained by normalizing the squared coupling:\n       $\\alpha_{body} = g_{body}^2 / \\Omega = (4/\\pi) / (4\\pi) = 1/\\pi^2$ .\n\n5. Part IV: The Regime-Conditional Framework\n\nThe Master Formula and RG Ladder\nDiscrepancies between $K_4$ predictions ( $v = 246 \\text{ GeV}$ ) and observation are\nresolved via the Regime-Conditional Formula: $$P_{obs}(\\mu) = P_{K4}(v) \\times\nC_{QCD}(\\mu/v) \\times C_{EW}(\\mu/v) \\times C_{grav}(\\mu/M_{Pl})$$ The IFS inverse levels\n\f( $n$ ) serve as the Renormalization Group (RG) ladder, where energy decades and threshold\ncrossings ( $\\Lambda_{QCD}$ ) occur between discrete ticks of the inverse IFS.\n\n$K_4$ Beta Function\nThe rate of QCD running is determined by the distinction number $\\Delta = 7$ : $b_0 =\n\\frac{33 - 12}{12\\pi} = \\frac{21}{12\\pi} = \\frac{7}{4\\pi} = \\frac{\\Delta}{4\\pi}$ .\n\nRegime Classification\nClass,Observables,Status\nA: Direct,\"$\\alpha_s$ , $n_s$ , $m_W$ , Leptons\",Validated ( $C \\approx 1$ )\nB: Small Regime,\"$\\theta_{12}$ , $m_H$ , $\\lambda$\",Validated ( $C \\approx 1 \\pm 10\\%$ )\nC: Large Regime,\"Quarks, Neutrinos, $\\delta_{CP}$\",Open (Requires explicit RG)\n\n6. Part V: Geometry, Simplicial Gravity, and F6 Results\n\nModified Gravitational Hamiltonian\nSimplicial gravity is injected into the OCPF Hamiltonian to account for curvature defects in the\n$\\delta^1$ channel: $$H_{grav} = -JK + \\lambda V + \\kappa \\cdot \\hat{R}{K_4}$$ where\n$\\kappa = 1/9\\pi^2$ and $\\hat{R}{K_4}$ is the Regge deficit angle operator.\n\nInflection and CC Resolution\nIn the $N=7$ monotone (null) run, the violation term ( $V$ ) acted as pure repulsion. Injecting\n$\\kappa$ introduces Geometric Attraction . The curvature defect $\\epsilon = \\pi$ creates a\npotential well pulling states toward the $K_4$ fixed point.\n    ●​ Inflection Point: $\\lambda/J \\approx 88.4$ .\n    ●​ Phase Shift: $f_{close}$ probability jumps from $0.34$ to $0.92$ .\n    ●​ Gravity serves as the \"Temporal Glue\" necessary to hold information together once the\n       $N=7$ partition threshold is exceeded.\n\n7. Part VI: The Unified Lepton Grammar\n\nSeed-and-Lift Operators\n   ●​ $S_0 = 43/7$ (Neutral-Seed Threshold): Six coherence slots plus a $1/7$ irreducible\n      remainder (formation memory).\n   ●​ $H = 101/6$ (Universal Lift): 16-node inherited scaffold plus 1 burden crossing, minus\n      a $1/6$ coherence reserve.\n\nThe Charged-Lepton Ladder\n   ●​ Electron ( $e$ ): $\\nu_0 S_0$\n   ●​ Muon ( $\\mu$ ): $e \\cdot S \\cdot H$ (where $S = 2S_0$ )\n   ●​ Tau ( $\\tau$ ): $e \\cdot S \\cdot H^2$| Ratio | UD Bare Form | Value | Observed |\n      Residual ( $z$ ) || ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ | ------ || $m_\\mu / m_e$ | $S \\cdot H$ | 207.21\n      | 206.77 | $\\approx -2 \\times 10^{-4}$ || $m_\\tau / m_\\mu$ | $H$ | 16.833 | 16.82 |\n\f       $\\approx -8 \\times 10^{-4}$ || $m_\\tau / m_e$ | $S \\cdot H^2$ | 3490.37 | 3477.15 |\n       $\\approx -1.5 \\times 10^{-3}$ |\n\n8. Part VII: Yin/Yang Regime Structure and Symmetry\nReality is defined by two interpenetrating sublattices of the diamond lattice:\n   ●​ $+1$ Regime (Matter): Positive action-cost, closure-entities, particle projection.\n   ●​ $-1$ Regime (Geometry): Mirror sector; sign-flipped operations are admissible.\n   ●​ Symmetry: This dual-sublattice structure provides the basis for CPT Symmetry and the\n        Dirac sea.\n   ●​ Charge: $q \\in \\{-1, 0, +1\\}$ is a direct projection of these regime sectors.\n\n9. Part VIII: The 28-Prediction Scorecard\nQuantity,Exact Form,Value,Status,Meaning\nMaster Scalar $x$,$7/192$,0.03646,Exact,Survival trace: $(1/2) \\cdot (7/16) \\cdot (1/6)$\nSpectral Index $n_s$,$185/192$,0.96354,Exact Bare,Bare CMB spectral tilt.\nTensor Ratio $r$,$7/192$,0.03646,Bare Spine (Falsified),Primordial GW amplitude (Exceeds\nbound <0.030).\nKoide Ratio $Q_K$,$2/3$,0.66667,Exact,Lepton triplet structural ratio.\nFine Structure $\\alpha_0^{-1}$,$960/7$,137.142,Candidate,Interaction intensity (x/5).\n$N=7$ Inflection,$\\lambda/J \\approx 88.4$,—,Confirmed,Matter-packet formation point.\n\n10. Part IX: Resolution of Gaps 1–7\n   ●​ Gap 1: Global closure via Banach fixed-point convergence.\n   ●​ Gap 2 (Red Tilt): Derived from $\\Omega$ -convergence. As $\\Omega$ converges to\n      1, power is imprinted on larger scales.\n   ●​ Gap 3 (Kinetic Term): Derived from the Genesis Action Cost $\\hbar_d$ . Making a\n      distinction is not free. In the slow-genesis limit, the absolute-value action $|\\dot{a}|$ of\n      the Poisson process reduces to the quadratic form $\\frac{1}{2}\\dot{a}^2$ .\n   ●​ Gap 5 (Fractal Dimension): $d_H \\approx 2.965$ confirmed via Box-Counting, Pair\n      Correlation ( $d_2$ ), and Mass-Radius. The 2D measurement ( $1.965$ ) is corrected\n      by the embedding factor ( $d_H(3D) = d_H(2D) + 1$ ).| Feature | Inflation | UD (\n      $\\Omega$ -Convergence) || ------ | ------ | ------ || Mathematical Basis | Potential flatness\n      | Banach Fixed-Point Theorem || Tensor Ratio | $16\\epsilon$ | $\\approx 0$ (IFS\n      contraction) |\n\n11. Part X: Conclusion and Artifact Registry\n\nThe Master Rule\n$Q_{obs} = Q_0(1 + z_Q)$ Reality is the weighted image of a typed operator grammar, where\nexact spines ( $Q_0$ ) are dressed by native accommodations ( $z_Q$ ).\n\nArtifact Index and Governance\n 1.​   Foundational Grammar: Seed $\\to$ threshold $\\to$ lift $\\to$ dressing.\n\f2.​   Corrected Einstein Block: $G_{\\mu\\nu} = \\kappaT_{GR} + \\Delta T_{\\theta, a, c, b}$ .\n3.​   Operator Core: $S_0 = 43/7, H = 101/6$ .\n4.​   Edit Propagation: Revisions to lower-tier artifacts ( $S_0$ ) necessitate recalculation of\n      all dependent lepton and oscillation artifacts. The $N=7$ inflection and $7/192$ ratio\n      are locked invariants.\n\f"
