    "content": "# UD OP03 receipt-index eligibility and typed-seat amendment v0.1\n\n**11 October 2026 UTC · development addendum · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Source hierarchy and question\n\n`UD_OPEN_SYSTEM_HAMMING_BUDGET_RECEIPT_INDEX_LAW_v0.2 (1).md` (30 August 2026, Library `libfile_8ea519b7af8881918c2d009ce74fe8d8`), §§1, 3–8, defines a conditional finite continuation index and a first-admissibility event rule. `UD_HAMMING_BUDGET_RECEIPT_INDEX_INDEPENDENT_AUDIT_v0.1.json` (30 August, `libfile_f8791a67b2a8819185cd7dd98d28504d`) independently reproduces rank and endpoint-optimizer algebra but explicitly says receipt construction and held-out performance remain conditional. `UD_OP03_INDEPENDENT_EVENT_ACQUISITION_PROTOCOL_v0.2_RECEIPT_INDEX.md` (4 September, `libfile_e56ff2964c8881918c6564d57e9a6a17`), §§Event boundary–Rollback, and its JSON schema (`libfile_65d6302675688191baefd0a7d73d6e20`) supersede the older v0.1 intake for receipt-index claims. `UD_OP03_AUTHENTICATED_HELD_OUT_REPLAY_SOURCE_GATE_v0.2.md` (14 September, `libfile_32f759d285608191a746627e198f7be7`), §§0–5, records source-blocked independent replay.\n\nThe previous [C1 frame-boundary capture](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-11T012338Z-codex-frame-boundary-fc4d4c2a) accurately scoped the frame extractor but did not account for the later v0.2 receipt-index event rule. This addendum **scope-amends** that remaining-gate statement. Its two tests ask whether the v0.2 rule distinguishes an executable null calculation from a switch, and whether a unique optimizer endpoint respects the independently typed output seat ledger.\n\n## Native (C_1) transport source boundary\n\nOn the filled oriented tetrahedron with Euclidean chain support metric, let (B_1:C_1\\to C_0), (B_2:C_2\\to C_1), and let (A) be the native skew Hodge–Dirac generator on (C_0\\oplus C_1\\oplus C_2\\oplus C_3). The attached `UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39(2).md`, Q169, is the source for the global generator (local SHA-256 `1281aa8454013fbbdbcf8ada07af0aefe81014003f25a27f3929ad43afffae63`). Direct incidence gives (B_1^TB_1+B_2B_2^T=4I_6). If (c_1\\in C_1) and (Ac_1\\in C_1), then (B_1c_1=0=B_2^Tc_1), hence\n\n\\[\n4\\lVert c_1\\rVert^2=\\lVert B_1c_1\\rVert^2+\\lVert B_2^Tc_1\\rVert^2=0,\n\\qquad c_1=0.\n\\]\n\n**EXACT, scoped:** the native 15-dimensional generator has no nonzero invariant subspace lying entirely inside (C_1). Consequently simply restricting this generator to an autonomous six-dimensional Markovian (C_1) state is unlawful. An operator action on six source-labelled probes could be recorded as a diagnostic, but compressing each step does not give the composed event transport: at (s=\\pi/4), (P_1e^{sA}\\iota_1=0_6), so the product of two compressed steps is (0_6), while (P_1e^{2sA}\\iota_1=-I_6). The [earlier projection audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-11T010749Z-codex-native-projection-c9c95ae7) has the same typed warning. This rules out the **naive Markovian restriction**, not every possible sourced (C_1) transfer or memory-enriched lineage construction.\n\n`UD_RELATIVE_FRAME_FROM_C1_EXECUTION_v0.7.md` (30 August, `libfile_197ff0fbc504819185ef21e9e3ed083f`), §§0–5, takes a source-complete pre-event (C_1) transfer as an input and extracts a frame when boundary covariance passes. The attached v0.39(2) global generator does not supply the missing native map from its coupled 15-dimensional evolution to that input. **OPEN_GATED:** give an actual ordered six-basis input/output action with source/target frames and history, or a memory/paired-history construction with its composition and lineage certificates. Keep the primitive local edge (U_e), chain compression, and frame residual distinct.\n\n## Counterexample 1: first admissibility can select a null self-loop\n\nWork in the fixed identity frame (r=e), with (\\Theta=\\mathbb F_2^3), (\\bar\\theta^-=000), pair-integrity (T=(1,1,1)), and source-complete coordinate obligations (\\mathcal L^-=\\mathcal L^+=\\operatorname{span}_{\\mathbb Q}(e_A,e_B,e_C)). Let the certified continuation be (F=I_3), with no novel source or renewal. Then (N_{sink}=N_{add}=0), (\\mu_\\Theta=0), (k^+=0). The exact shell consists only of (000), for **any** finite quadratic burden score. The v0.2 §8 frame, index, feasibility, and singleton gates all pass, but\n\n\\[\n\\theta^+=\\bar\\theta^-=000,\\quad c_\\Theta=o_\\Theta=a_\\Theta=000,\\quad U^\\Theta=I_8.\n\\]\n\n**EXACT counterexample to the wording “first executable event” as first Θ switch:** the printed v0.2 minimization can select this no-op at the first candidate (n). The arithmetic map remains valid; the occurrence claim needs a nontriviality condition. The proposed **CANDIDATE v0.2.1** distinction is `ADMISSIBLE_NO_CHANGE` when (a_\\Theta=000), and a parity-switch event only when (a_\\Theta\\ne000). This tests an already predicted affine receipt; it adds no amplitude threshold. For a full exposure update, independently record whether (r\\ne e); a frame-only update must have its own event type. Zero budget (\\mu=0) cannot serve as a no-event guard because a two-seat swap has (a_\\Theta\\ne000) at zero net Hamming change.\n\n## Counterexample 2: rank does not fix the typed pair address\n\nLet (\\bar\\theta^-=100); the open seats are B and C. Let (\\mathcal L^-=\\mathcal L^+=\\operatorname{span}_{\\mathbb Q}(e_B,e_C)), (F=I_2), no additions, all pair-integrity receipts one. This is a coordinate-tagged, source-complete continuation, so (\\mu=0), (k^+=1) and **B,C remain the two viable open obligations**. As a concrete exact burden diagnostic in the §2.3 form of `UD_OP03_JOINT_REPLAY_EXECUTION_v0.9.md` (4 September, `libfile_de1a3ebc085c8191a78c966bd723cd7a`), take the K4 vertex burden (b=(0,2,1,3)). Squared incidence gradients on the opposite pairs (A=(01,23)), (B=(02,13)), (C=(03,12)) give (W=(8,2,10)).\n\nThe v0.2 §7 objective minimizes (\\sum_p\\theta_p W_p) over the weight-one shell. It uniquely returns (\\theta^+=010), because (2<8<10), and the affine toggle is (a=110). But that endpoint opens A,C and **closes the surviving B obligation** while opening A without a source or renewal. All v0.2 listed integrity and singleton gates pass. Of the six distinct rankings of three scores, four similarly choose an endpoint inconsistent with the frozen B,C output seats. These are exact finite diagnostics, not event observations or frequencies.\n\n**NO-GO under the seat-faithful source reading:** the v0.2 shell plus burden objective cannot universally turn a typed output-obligation space into a compatible endpoint. If (\\mathcal L^+\\) is instead meant to specify only a rank and not seat addresses, its relation to the source document's pair-seat images remains **OPEN**. Either interpretation blocks unconditional source-complete pair-address promotion.\n\n**CANDIDATE v0.2.1 typed repair:** when frozen receipts give a coordinate subspace (\\mathcal L^+\\), restrict the feasible shell by\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{span}\\{e_p:\\theta_p=0\\}=\\mathcal L^+.\n\\]\n\nFor non-coordinate lineages, freeze an explicit lineage-to-seat assignment or return `RECEIPT_SEAT_MAP_MISSING`. On coordinate-complete receipts the equality selects exactly one endpoint, so the burden objective becomes a consistency diagnostic rather than an address chooser. The optimizer can decide among endpoints only if an independently sourced admissible assignment set leaves genuine alternatives. This is a proposed versioned amendment, **not** an overwrite or AUTO_LOCK of v0.2.\n\nA true zero-budget swap remains allowed when tagged receipts say (\\mathcal L^+=\\operatorname{span}(e_A,e_C)), with a B sink and independent A addition: then (\\theta^+=010), (a=110), and (\\mu=1-1=0). This separates gross turnover, endpoint change, and net Hamming budget without conflating their carriers.\n\n## Independent acquisition workload\n\nThe v0.2 receipt-index acquisition protocol and authenticated source gate require independent producer identity, pre-frozen (C_1) action, lineage/seat map, viability and burden receipts, prediction hash before access, and sealed endpoint frame/Θ. A current Library title/content search for OP03 histories and sealed endpoints surfaced protocols, synthetic controls, and the v0.2 source-blocked gate; targeted code searches on the UD GitHub default branch for `pre_event.jsonl`, `outcomes.jsonl`, `observed_theta_plus`, `lineage_equivalence_receipts`, and `sealed` returned no matches. Those search scopes do not prove global nonexistence. The previously documented v0.9 corpus is synthetic and does not exercise the v0.2 receipt-index law (`UD_OP03_JOINT_REPLAY_AND_RECEIPT_INDEX_RECONCILIATION_v0.1.md`, `libfile_ad8e43dd4cb48191936989f9069ed00e`, §§Receipt-index–Next replay).\n\n**NO_DATA / NOT_RUN:** no independent endpoints were exposed and no frozen OP03 scorer was run. The v0.2 protocol remains the intake, with this addendum's null and seat-compatibility findings frozen **before any future target exposure**. If targets already existed elsewhere, the amendment must be treated as exploratory against those targets; a fresh independently governed cohort would be required for a confirmatory test.\n\n## Disposition and reopening conditions\n\n**EXACT:** the (C_1) non-invariance and compression-composition obstruction; both finite v0.2 counterexamples under stated coordinate-seat assumptions; rank-nullity index identity is preserved. **CANDIDATE:** v0.2.1 no-op event typing and seat-compatibility gate. **OPEN_GATED:** native source-complete (C_1) producer or lawful paired history, independent typed lineage-to-seat construction, and independently sealed target history. No external physical correspondence or predictive validation is established. Physical promotion remains 0, independent review pending.\n"
