    "content": "# OP03 independent-producer acquisition decision v0.1\n\n**11 October 2026 UTC · development — no registry entry · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Result\n\n**SOURCE_BLOCKED / NOT_RUN.** No independently governed producer and no sealed full-frame/\\(\\Theta\\) endpoint cohort was obtained from the inspected sources. The v0.2 purpose-built bench archive is a prepared acquisition contract, not observations. This is an acquisition finding, not a negative test of the OP03 switch rule.\n\n## Source inspection\n\nThe current [OP03 source-boundary capture](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-11T015458Z-codex-source-bridge-8e19b473), `REPORT.md` §§Conditional 12D-to-6D frame certificate–Acquisition and freeze status, and `INPUT_CONTRACT_v0.1_CANDIDATE.md` freeze the typed pre-event inputs. The frozen `UD_OP03_INDEPENDENT_EVENT_ACQUISITION_PROTOCOL_v0.2_RECEIPT_INDEX.md` (30 August 2026, Library `libfile_e56ff2964c8881918c6564d57e9a6a17`), “Pre-event frame packet” through “Hidden target packet,” requires independent pre-event receipts and separately hidden full frame/\\(\\Theta\\) endpoints. `UD_OP03_AUTHENTICATED_HELD_OUT_REPLAY_SOURCE_GATE_v0.2.md` (14 September, `libfile_32f759d285608191a746627e198f7be7`), §§0–5, reports source-blocked status. The older [two-stage intake](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165944Z-codex-op03-intake-ed488bce) scores only conditional one-pair capacity polarity; it is not a full frame/seat/timing scorer.\n\nThe Library file `UD_OP03_KBS_PURPOSE_BUILT_BENCH_v0.2.zip` (18 September, `libfile_ceb05c2a86308191a6244df532953d03`, SHA-256 `e1fb3c2c53ce7caf50bcf748d1d211fee4e39a379e116d895c3d8e57d7cb9b65`) was opened. Its `README.md` states `NO REAL EVENTS`, and `protocol/V0_2_STATE.json` records `real_events: 0`. Its `contracts/EVENT_ENGINE_HANDOFF_CONTRACT.md` requires an independently authored engine and a pre-acquisition hash; `templates/ENGINE_COMMIT_TEMPLATE.json` remains a placeholder. The archive has scripts, schemas, templates and labeled synthetic controls, with no provider return that could constitute a sealed event. The nested `protocol/UD_OP03_DUAL_LANE_ACQUISITION_v0.1.zip` (SHA-256 `1edce616734021ff780ab3a6a759b5b4c3ab4cbf692eec6ef05c28486b1aba17`) records `current_real_event_count: 0` and `synthetic_controls_only: true` in `ACQUISITION_MANIFEST.json`.\n\n**Typed crosswalk:** the nested dual-lane bench is designed for \\(\\Xi^{FH}\\stackrel{?}{=}\\operatorname{sgn}G_\\Sigma^{S\\pm}\\), taking an ordered latent/integrity \\(L/T\\) source history as target. Even a future qualifying run of that lane would not automatically supply independently observed full \\(r\\), \\(\\theta^+\\), pair address and null-window timing required for the full v0.2/v0.2.1 OP03 claim. Equal pair indices do not make these targets the same object. Its potential one-pair evidence must be scoped to its own claim.\n\nThe targeted 11 October Library title and UD GitHub default-branch code searches documented in the [previous acquisition status](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-11T015458Z-codex-source-bridge-8e19b473/ACQUISITION_STATUS.json) found no additional qualified cohort. Searches and this archive inspection cannot rule out private or unpublished producer material.\n\n## Executable handoff boundary\n\n`PROVIDER_HANDOFF_v0.1.md` specifies the outside producer's source and target returns, chronological seal, and the exact ineligible cases. It is a request specification ready to hand to a provider; no provider was contacted and no attestation, code hash, raw window, hidden target, score or independent adversarial review was received. If existing records are already target-exposed, the v0.2.1 seat/no-op amendment can only be evaluated exploratorily on them; use a fresh cohort for confirmation.\n\n## Disposition\n\n**EXACT source audit:** the inspected archives declare zero real events and include no provider event return. **OPEN:** an independently authored source and event engine, target-independent eligibility, all consecutive pre-event and null windows, separate sealed full frame and \\(\\Theta\\) endpoints, and non-constructor review. The attached `UD_GOVERNANCE_CRL2_SUBDIVISION_v1.0.md`, §§1–4, is a proposal; constructor work does not promote a bridge past CRL-2a. Physical promotion 0.\n"
