    "content": "# Record entropy and receipt apparatus — session capture\n\nDevelopment — no registry entry. Physical promotion: 0. Independent review: OPEN.\n\nThis capture preserves twelve original releases, their proofs, replay receipts and a portal/GitHub cross-reference. It covers the available mathematical session artifacts; it is not a verbatim export of all chat messages. Unavailable Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png is not included or used. Credentials, private helper state and unrelated personal context are excluded.\n\nDeclared coarse-graining yields record entropies, but a universal horizon-area law and its physical normalization remain OPEN. No Newton constant is used to calibrate the entropy density. Native snapshot entropy need not increase; accumulated trajectory entropy is a different quantity.\n\nThe five-tetrahedron complex has 47 simplices and 12 exposed faces. One carrier with 13 boundary outcomes cannot supply an extensive independent memory per face. The 12-bit Gibbs memory, thermal collisions, ground encoding, local write controls, bath renewal, fault flags and receipt majority are explicitly declared candidate apparatus extensions.\n\nThe joint receipt error state is (1-c) Bern(p)^tensor3 + c complemented Bern(p)^tensor3. Its pair moment is a=p^2+c(1-2p); majority error is m=(3p^2-2p^3)+c[1-2(3p^2-2p^3)]. At p=0.01 and independent decision q=0.0001, the robust common-flag ceiling is approximately 0.00002567950424 and the exact-model ceiling approximately 0.00007796483800, for the previously declared 32-update storage interval and 1% final-error gate.\n\nComplete resource accounting remains OPEN: the memory-cycle lower bounds do not include a closed, renewed controller and bath. Ideal Gibbs swaps transfer correlations to outgoing bath systems. The explicit flag implementation requires 34 write gates and 23 holding updates, so its 32-update post-write test is a 66-slot schedule, not the earlier 44-slot comparison.\n\nNative source selection of app