nk certificate An incidence is an ordered pair (σ,η)(\\sigma,\\eta) with σ\\sigma a codimension-one face of η\\eta. With the inherited orientation sign bσηb_{\\sigma\\eta}, AX=∑(σ,η)∈ℐXbση(eηeσT−eσeηT). A_X=\\sum_{(\\sigma,\\eta)\\in\\mathcal I_X} b_{\\sigma\\eta}(e_\\eta e_\\sigma^T-e_\\sigma e_\\eta^T). The same formula with ambient coordinate columns expresses the lifted operators. Consequently, ΔA\\Delta A is the sum of the created incidence terms minus the deleted incidence terms. There are 36 common, 11 removed, and 23 created incidences. Thus ΔA\\Delta A has 68 nonzero entries, all ±1\\pm1. Every nonzero entry touches at least one changed simplex. The common-common block is zero. This does not mean only changed-coordinate rows are affected: an incidence can join a changed simplex to a retained one. There are 27 nonzero rows; only the vertex rows 0,1,20,1,2 vanish. Proposition 2 (rank of the update). rankℚΔA=rankℝΔA=18,dimkerΔA=12. \\boxed{\\operatorname{rank}_{\\mathbb Q}\\Delta A =\\operatorname{rank}_{\\mathbb R}\\Delta A=18,\\qquad \\dim\\ker\\Delta A=12.} Exact finite certificate. Reorder coordinates by even and odd simplex degree. Both parts have dimension 15, and ΔA∼(0W−WT0),rankW=9. \\Delta A\\sim\\begin{pmatrix}0&W\\\\-W^T&0\\end{pmatrix}, \\qquad \\operatorname{rank}W=9. Independently, the principal minor on the following 18 labeled coordinates has determinant one: (3,01,03,13,23,34,012,013,014,023,034,123,134,234,0123,0124,0134,0234). (3,01,03,13,23,34,012,013,014,023,034,123,134,234, 0123,0124,0134,0234). This gives rank at least 18. The supplied 30×1230\\times12 rational matrix NN satisfies ΔAN=0\\Delta A N=0 and has twelve independent columns, giving rank at most 18. Its free-coordinate rows form an identity matrix by construction. Both multiplication and the determinant are reproduced exactly by the verifier. ▫\\square Rank 18 is not a claim that the update is tiny relative to this 30-dimensional example. It is a bounded local update: placing this valid local replacement in a larger complex, without additional changed incidences, extends this difference by zeros and preserves its rank. No claim is made that global spectra are direct sums of the local spectra. 4. Integer homology and the oriented boundary survivor Proposition 3. Both K−K_- and K+K_+ have H0≅ℤH_0\\cong\\mathbb Z and vanishing reduced integer homology. They have the identical labeled exterior boundary CC and admit oriented fundamental chains with exactly the same boundary. Integral certificate. The minus complex is a cone with apex 0; the plus complex is a cone with apex 3. For the appropriate apex vv, define the signed cone map hh by adjoining vv to each simplex not already containing it, ordering the result increasingly, and assigning sign (−1)j(-1)^j, where jj is the insertion position. Set it to zero on simplices containing vv. The integer matrices satisfy DXh+hDX=I−Pv, D_Xh+hD_X=I-P_v, where PvP_v sends every vertex to vv and annihilates higher degrees. The supplied matrices verify this identity, proving the integer assertion, including absence of torsion. Rational Betti numbers alone would not establish that conclusion. Take t−=0123−0124,t+=−0134+0234−1234. t_-=0123-0124,\\qquad t_+=-0134+0234-1234. Both boundaries are b=013−014−023+024+123−124. b=013-014-023+024+123-124. Moreover, ι−t−−ι+t+=1234−0234+0134−0124+0123=:zU. \\iota_-t_- -\\iota_+t_+ =1234-0234+0134-0124+0123=:z_U. This is the primitive top cycle of ∂Δ4\\partial\\Delta^4, with DUzU=0D_Uz_U=0. It generates H3(U;ℤ)≅ℤH_3(U;\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\mathbb Z. Thus the two filling chains agree on their boundary but do not become homologous in the chosen 3-dimensional ambient. Adding the 4-simplex would kill this difference, but would change the declared ambient and is not done here. ▫\\square The common exterior boundary survives the move. The expression “boundary of UU” must not be used for it: UU is closed and has empty manifold boundary. 5. Exact native and lifted spectra Multiplicities below are denoted by superscripts. Since each AXA_X is real skew-symmetric, positive eigenvalues of LX=−AX2L_X=-A_X^2 correspond to imaginary conjugate eigenvalue pairs of AXA_X. Operator Exact spectrum of its negative square A−A_-, dimension 23 0[1],3[8],5[14]0^{[1]},3^{[8]},5^{[14]} A+A_+, dimension 27 0[1],2[4],5[22]0^{[1]},2^{[4]},5^{[22]} A−UA_-^U, dimension 30 0[8],3[8],5[14]0^{[8]},3^{[8]},5^{[14]} A+UA_+^U, dimension 30 0[4],2[4],5[22]0^{[4]},2^{[4]},5^{[22]} AUA_U, dimension 30 0[2],5[28]0^{[2]},5^{[28]} Equivalently, χA−(λ)=λ(λ2+3)4(λ2+5)7,χA+(λ)=λ(λ2+2)2(λ2+5)11, \\chi_{A_-}(\\lambda)=\\lambda(\\lambda^2+3)^4(\\lambda^2+5)^7, \\qquad \\chi_{A_+}(\\lambda)=\\lambda(\\lambda^2+2)^2(\\lambda^2+5)^{11}, χA−U(λ)=λ8(λ2+3)4(λ2+5)7,χA+U(λ)=λ4(λ2+2)2(λ2+5)11, \\chi_{A_-^U}(\\lambda)=\\lambda^8(\\lambda^2+3)^4(\\lambda^2+5)^7, \\qquad \\chi_{A_+^U}(\\lambda)=\\lambda^4(\\lambda^2+2)^2(\\lambda^2+5)^{11}, χAU(λ)=λ2(λ2+5)14. \\chi_{A_U}(\\lambda)=\\lambda^2(\\lambda^2+5)^{14}. Finite proof and verification. The boundary ranks are (4,5,2)(4,5,2), (4,6,3)(4,6,3), and (4,6,4)(4,6,4) for minus, plus, and ambient. The verifier checks exact annihilating identities L−(L−−3I)(L−−5I)=0,L+(L+−2I)(L+−5I)=0,LU(LU−5I)=0, L_-(L_--3I)(L_--5I)=0,\\qquad L_+(L_+-2I)(L_+-5I)=0,\\qquad L_U(L_U-5I)=0, as well as exact eigenspace nullities. Symmetry of LL makes these eigenspaces complete; their dimensions sum to the matrix sizes. The traces 94,118,14094,118,140, respectively, also agree with twice the incidence counts. Padding adds exactly seven and three zero coordinates. These extra zero modes are not the homology of UU. The spectra are recorded as separate correctly typed polynomials and as spectra of two 30-dimensional lifts. No subtraction of unequal-degree characteristic polynomials is used as an operator update. 6. Incidence receipts and reference forests Receipts refer here only to real coordinate stocks and signed incidence products: qσ=cσ2,Jση=2bσηcσcη. q_\\sigma=c_\\sigma^