rgy or integrated transfer. These channels are algebraic incidences; they are not yet spatial tubes with a derived transport velocity or cross-sectional area. For a declared regular tetrahedron of physical edge length ℓ, intrinsic measures could be 1, ℓ, √3ℓ²/4, and ℓ³/(6√2). No physical value of ℓ is selected here. Densities on different-dimensional supports cannot simply be added to form a volumetric energy density. A flux density in W/m² also needs a specified spatial surface and transport map. For the isolated native tetrahedron, the incidence norm gives |Pk,k+1|≤4τ⋆EkEk+1≤2τ⋆(Ek+Ek+1). |P_{k,k+1}|\\le\\frac4{\\tau_\\star}\\sqrt{E_kE_{k+1}} \\le\\frac2{\\tau_\\star}(E_k+E_{k+1}). This coefficient belongs to that operator; it is not asserted for arbitrary complexes. Energy stocks alone do not fix power: cross-degree signed correlations are required. Ensemble powers use the raw moments ⟨cσcη⟩ in the same formula. 4. Hamiltonian closure and a mechanical interpretation Define the constant Poisson matrix 𝕁=A2E⋆τ⋆=A2𝒜⋆,{F,G}=(∇F)T𝕁∇G. \\mathbb J=\\frac{A}{2E_\\star\\tau_\\star} =\\frac{A}{2\\mathcal A_\\star},\\qquad \\{F,G\\}=(\\nabla F)^T\\mathbb J\\nabla G. Its skewness and constant entries give antisymmetry and the Jacobi identity. With E1, dcdt=𝕁∇H=1τ⋆Ac. \\boxed{\\frac{dc}{dt}=\\mathbb J\\nabla H=\\frac1{\\tau_\\star}Ac.} Thus the adopted energy is a Hamiltonian for the retained flow under this explicitly constructed bracket. The factor two follows from differentiating cᵀc; it is not a new coupling. This construction demonstrates consistency, not independent physical selection of the bracket or Hamiltonian. For one tetrahedron, let h=(1,1,1,1,0,…,0)ᵀ/2. The harmonic amplitude hᵀc is a Casimir: it is fixed by this Poisson flow. The full 15-dimensional bracket is degenerate, of rank 14. On each active leaf, with Q=I−hhᵀ, the inverse two-form is Ω=−𝒜⋆2A,Ω𝕁=𝕁Ω=Q. \\Omega=-\\frac{\\mathcal A_\\star}{2}A,\\qquad \\Omega\\mathbb J=\\mathbb J\\Omega=Q. For active coordinates x=Qc and fixed harmonic amplitude, the first-order action I[x]=∫(12xTΩẋ−E⋆xTx)dt I[x]=\\int\\left(\\tfrac12x^T\\Omega\\dot x-E_\\star x^Tx\\right)dt yields the active flow. The harmonic energy is constant on a leaf and can be added without changing that variation. This is an action for the present sector; it is not a recovered UD master action or a quantum action normalization. Each nonzero real skew mode can be written ξ̇=−ντ⋆η,η̇=ντ⋆ξ,Hν=E⋆(ξ2+η2). \\dot\\xi=-\\frac\\nu{\\tau_\\star}\\eta, \\qquad\\dot\\eta=\\frac\\nu{\\tau_\\star}\\xi, \\qquad H_\\nu=E_\\star(\\xi^2+\\eta^2). With q=ξ, p=−2𝒜★η/ν, the bracket is canonical and Hν=p22𝖬+12𝖬ω2q2,𝖬=2E⋆τ⋆2ν2,ω=ντ⋆. H_\\nu=\\frac{p^2}{2\\mathsf M}+\\frac12\\mathsf M\\omega^2q^2, \\quad\\mathsf M=\\frac{2E_\\star\\tau_\\star^2}{\\nu^2}, \\quad\\omega=\\frac\\nu{\\tau_\\star}. This gives a precise oscillator interpretation with storage exchanged between two quadratures. Since q is dimensionless, 𝕄 has units J·s² and is a generalized inertia, not a derived mass in kilograms. A displacement identification Qphysical=ℓq would introduce another declared mapping and inertia 𝕄/ℓ². No such physical displacement or particle assignment is made. The isolated active frequency is ν=2; the glued pair has ν=√3,√5. No energy-frequency quantization rule follows. In particular, neither E=ℏω nor E=mc² has been used to assign a packet energy or mass. 5. Locality, gluing, and ownership For any subset of simplex coordinates R, let ER=Σσ∈R Eσ. Internal incidence powers cancel pairwise, leaving exactly power entering across the incidence cut minus power leaving. This is a control-volume balance on the discrete carrier; spatial interpretation of that cut remains a separate map. Shared vertices, edges, and faces must not be counted twice when tetrahedra are glued. If cell ownership is needed, the retained equal-ownership convention is wσ,τ={1/n3(σ),σ⊆τ,0,otherwise,Eτowned=∑σwσ,τEσ. w_{\\sigma,\\tau}=\\begin{cases}1/n_3(\\sigma),&\\sigma\\subseteq\\tau,\\\\0,&\\text{otherwise},\\end{cases} \\qquad E_\\tau^{\\mathrm{owned}}=\\sum_\\sigma w_{\\sigma,\\tau}E_\\sigma. For the complexes here, summing over cells recovers H. Its derivative is the weighted incidence sum Σσ⊂η (wη,τ−wσ,τ)Pσ→η. This follows by weighting the verified simplex balances. The owned-cell energy differs from the cell-core energy E★c3,τ². Equal ownership is a bookkeeping convention; it is not a newly derived spatial energy localization law. The no-cascade theorem remains in force. Changing the name or units of the conserved stock does not let a pure vertex launch reach faces or cells under the fixed chain flow. All earlier launch predictions convert by Ek=E★Sk, Pkl=(E★/τ★)Jkl, and s=t/τ★. 6. External inputs, reservoirs, dissipation, and resets The following are typed interfaces around the closed sector, not newly selected UD mechanisms. Reciprocal reservoir. Give reservoir amplitudes b the same energy normalization and specify a dimensionless coupling matrix C: ċ=(Ac+Cb)/τ⋆,ḃ=(−CTc+Abb)/τ⋆,AbT=−Ab. \\dot c=(Ac+Cb)/\\tau_\\star,\\qquad \\dot b=(-C^Tc+A_b b)/\\tau_\\star,\\qquad A_b^T=-A_b. Then Htotal=E★(||c||²+||b||²) is conserved and Ḣc=2E⋆τ⋆cTCb=−Ḣb. \\dot H_c=\\frac{2E_\\star}{\\tau_\\star}c^TCb=-\\dot H_b. These added coordinates are reservoir storage amplitudes, not additional spatial dimensions. Their purpose is to supply the missing exchange partner. Under orthogonal basis changes they transform with their own carrier, and C transforms as a map from reservoir to packet. Setting C=0 recovers the isolated model. The replay uses one reservoir coordinate and a port at the first vertex as an explicitly addressed diagnostic; this is not a symmetry-derived natural selector. Any physically proposed C, reservoir preparation, and port location need their own source provenance. Forcing and dissipation. For a specified forcing f with units s⁻¹ and dimensionless symmetric positive-semidefinite R, ċ=(A−R)c/τ⋆+f,Ḣ=Pext−Pdiss,Pext=2E⋆cTf,Pdiss=2E⋆τ⋆cTRc≥0. \\dot c=(A-R)c/\\tau_\\star+f, \\quad \\dot H=P_{\\mathrm{ext}}-P_{\\mathrm{diss}}, \\quad P_{\\mathrm{ext}}=2E_\\star c^Tf, \\quad P_{\\mathrm{diss}}=\\frac{2E_\\star}{\\tau_\\star}c^TRc\\ge0. Account for dissipated energy in an unresolved reservoir ledger, dEunresolved/dt=Pdiss, so d(H+Eunresolved)/dt=Pext. Calling that reservoir heat requires thermal degrees of freedom and a thermodynamic interpretation; this identity alone supplies neither temperature nor entropy production. No damping rate is adopted in the reversible UD branch. State resets. If c+=T c−, the required event receipt is ΔH=E⋆(c−)T(TTT−I)c−. \\Delta H=E_\\star(c^-)^T(T^TT-I)c^-. Positive values require supplied energy; negative values must be allocated to an output/reservoir. A renormalization is not automatically an energy-neutral physical operation. If it only changes coordinates, the energy metric must transform too. As an exact diagnostic, attenuation T=(3/5)I retains 9/25 of the energy. An orthogonal packet-reservoir rotation with complementary amplitude 4/5 transfers 16/25 to an initially empty reservoir, conserving the parent energy. These fractions are chosen test controls, not predicted UD coefficients or a natural attenuation law. The new reservoir coordinate reduces to the original sector when the exchange is disabled. 7. Gates and changing energy definitions A gate modifying only the skew matrix A(t) leaves E1 conserved pointwise when c is continuous: cᵀA(t)c=0. This is an ideal lossless modulation model for the packet energy. It does not prove that a physical gate controller consumes no energy. An actual controller must have its own Hamiltonian or measured/sourced work ledger; those inputs cannot be inferred from skewness. The previous face-gate audit remains binding: holding B1,B2 fixed, all 128 binary face-row masks conserve stock, but only the all-zero and all-one masks preserve the chain identity on the glued pair. Energy conservation does not repair the other 126 c