ndently constructed Hodge operator. The supplied five-seat response ratio 5/65/6 is not imported as a kinetic/potential ratio without a map establishing that interpretation. 7. What comes next Review target Evidence needed A nontrivial reciprocal event Source-defined forward and reverse maps, recorded through an executable runtime interface. Rate and normalization Signed directional slopes, convergence and symmetry checks, then a pulled-back storage check. A selected event action A source statement fixing the quadratic coefficients and coordinate convention. An event/Hodge identification An independently constructed map preserving the specified dynamical and symplectic structures. The upload supplies 20 files. Two earlier files complete its three manifests, giving 22 preserved originals and 16 matching manifest references. This batch is complete against those manifests. It does not supply the four missing references named in the previous review. The reproduction supplement contains exact symbolic checks, the isolated zero-fixture replay and unchanged originals. Historical source searches are the authors’ reported audits; they were not independently repeated in this review. No acquired physical session or physical identification is claimed. Preserved source documents Protocol and implementation Finite algebra and candidate symmetries Source Addendum Event S5 Neutral Natural Cotangent Lift — original Event Internal U1 Source Audit — original Event Source Action And Target Blind U1 Audit — original Manuscript Addendum Normalization Rate Repair — original Manuscript Addendum S5 Cotangent And Runtime Microreceipt — original Reciprocal Raw Transfer Factor Identification — original Support Burden Normalization Coupling Rate Repair — original Historical source audits and controls Bidirectional Fg Methodology Validation Result — original Bidirectional Support Burden Current Runtime Probe — original Bidirectional Support Burden Current Runtime Result — original Bidirectional 