=12(m0Δq0,e+m⊥Δq⊥,e). \\boxed{ \\Delta_eH_B = \\frac12 \\left( m_0\\Delta q_{0,e} + m_\\perp\\Delta q_{\\perp,e} \\right). } For a closed nondissipative conversion event, m0Δq0,e+m⊥Δq⊥,e=−2ΔeHS. \\boxed{ m_0\\Delta q_{0,e} + m_\\perp\\Delta q_{\\perp,e} = -2\\Delta_eH_S. } 5. One-event identifiability theorem A generic single event supplies one scalar equation for the two unknown metric coefficients m0,m⊥. m_0,\\ m_\\perp. Therefore a mixed-sector event cannot uniquely determine the full K4 burden metric. AUTO_LOCK ONE_MIXED_GATE_TO_BURDEN_EVENT_CANNOT_IDENTIFY_BOTH_K4_BURDEN_METRIC_SECTORS_v0.1 6. Sector-isolating closure routes Uniform-only event If Δq⊥,e=0 \\Delta q_{\\perp,e}=0 and Δq0,e≠0, \\Delta q_{0,e}\\neq0, then m0=−2ΔeHSΔq0,e \\boxed{ m_0 = -\\frac{2\\Delta_eH_S}{\\Delta q_{0,e}} } for a closed nondissipative event. Contrast-only event If Δq0,e=0 \\Delta q_{0,e}=0 and Δq⊥,e≠0, \\Delta q_{\\perp,e}\\neq0, then m⊥=−2ΔeHSΔq⊥,e. \\boxed{ m_\\perp = -\\frac{2\\Delta_eH_S}{\\Delta q_{\\perp,e}}. } Thus two independent sector-isolating same-event receipts would be sufficient to identify MB=m0P0+m⊥P⊥ \\boxed{ M_B=m_0P_0+m_\\perp P_\\perp } without target fitting. AUTO_LOCK — conditional TWO_SECTOR_ISOLATING_GATE_TO_BURDEN_RECEIPTS_CAN_IDENTIFY_K4_RAW_BURDEN_METRIC_v0.1 7. Q173 cannot be silently reused as support-storage loss Current hard-gated support receipt J23h=2hfB3,fτc2,fc3,τ J_{23}^h = 2h_fB_{3,f\\tau}c_{2,f}c_{3,\\tau} is an internal support throughput object. It transfers support between support-chain degrees. By itself it does not establish a net loss of total support storage: ΔeHS<0. \\Delta_eH_S<0. Therefore it cannot serve as the support-loss leg of the gate→burden receipt without an additional source/sink theorem. AUTO_LOCK Q173_GATE_TRANSITION_CURRENT_IS_NOT_BY_ITSELF_SUPPORT_STORAGE_LOSS_v0.1 8. Q158 cannot be silently reused as gate-generated burden Current sB=Δρ−B1jB s_B = \\Delta\\rho-B_1j_B is a residual burden source receipt. Its predictive constitutive source remains open. Therefore it cannot be identified with the burden-gain leg of the gate event without a common-event tag. AUTO_LOCK Q158_BURDEN_RESIDUAL_IS_NOT_BY_ITSELF_GATE_TO_BURDEN_CONVERSION_v0.1 9. Same-event tagging requirement A lawful gate→burden source packet must carry the same event identifier on: support storage change; burden state change; external input receipt; dissipation receipt; gate transition state. Without that common tag, temporal coincidence is insufficient to infer conversion. 10. Relation to the primitive KXK_X generator A finite same-event receipt can determine storage conversion and, with enough independent events, the metric MBM_B. It does not by itself determine the infinitesimal exchange generator KXK_X. To identify KXK_X, one additionally needs immediate directional response telemetry or a source law for the event rate. Thus: same-event storage receipt⇒MBcandidate \\boxed{ \\text{same-event storage receipt} \\Rightarrow M_B\\ \\text{candidate} } but not automatically KX. K_X. 11. Adversarial verdict Mathematical structure PASS. Current-source instantiation FAIL / OPEN. Current source has separately typed support throughput and burden source receipts, but no common-event storage-conversion identity. Candidate status 𝚂𝙾𝚄𝚁𝙲𝙴_𝙰𝙳𝙳𝙴𝙽𝙳𝚄𝙼_𝙶𝙰𝚃𝙴_𝚃𝙾_𝙱𝚄𝚁𝙳𝙴𝙽_𝙴𝚇𝙲𝙷𝙰𝙽𝙶𝙴_𝚁𝙴𝙲𝙴𝙸𝙿𝚃_𝚟𝟶.𝟷 \\boxed{ \\texttt{SOURCE\\_ADDENDUM\\_GATE\\_TO\\_BURDEN\\_EXCHANGE\\_RECEIPT\\_v0.1} } = 𝙲𝙰𝙽𝙳𝙸𝙳𝙰𝚃𝙴 / 𝙿𝚁𝙴𝚁𝙴𝙶𝙸𝚂𝚃𝙴𝚁𝙰𝙱𝙻𝙴 / 𝙽𝙾𝚃 𝙰𝙳𝙼𝙸𝚃𝚃𝙴𝙳 \\boxed{ \\texttt{CANDIDATE / PREREGISTERABLE / NOT ADMITTED} } 12. Falsifiers Reject the conversion hypothesis if a tagged event shows: burden gain without corresponding support loss or declared external input; support loss without burden gain or declared dissipation; no positive MBM_B can satisfy repeated receipts; inferred m0,m⊥m_0,m_\\perp depend on probe amplitude/history in the claimed linear regime; event tags reveal that support and burden changes come from distinct source events. Physical promotion: 0."
