    "content": "Conditional conservation, revised acquisition requirements and exact symmetry checks. The analyzer is a slope helper; no acquired event is claimed. Event exchange, metric identification and parity Supporting mathematical and protocol review · 19 September 2026 The new material separates three questions: what a proposed event conserves, which measurements identify its quadratic storage metric, and what additional symmetry would distinguish two three-dimensional state sectors. It improves the acquisition specification and narrows the unresolved source requirements. It does not supply a measured event, a derived event-source law, or an identification with a physical field. The finite theorem statements remain in Paper I and Paper II. This review concerns conditional extensions. “Burden” here means an auxiliary finite vector with a specified quadratic storage function; no physical energy or action unit is assigned. Download the review and reproduction supplement · Independent verification results · Source inventory What has advanced Question Current result Remaining requirement Can one event identify a storage metric? A mixed scalar balance supplies one equation. Two independent sector equations can identify a two-parameter metric. Eligible, attributable observations and the stated symmetry assumption. Does the revised protocol isolate the event? Version 0.2 specifies matched controls, directional receipts, a fixed region and event timing. Independent protocol review and an implementation that enforces those requirements. Can reciprocal exchange conserve total storage? Yes, for an explicitly supplied skew block generator. Evidence selecting that generator and its coefficients. Does tetrahedral symmetry select a parity? The tested gradient/cycle and Hodge-star constructions have precise representation limits. A paired standard sector permits a swap. A source-selected involution compatible with the relevant action. Has the acquisition been completed? No acquired session is supplied in this package. Qualified source data, frozen scoring and independent replay. 1. Start with the accounting model Let cc be the real support coordinates in a fixed region and b∈ℝ4b\\in\\mathbb R^4 the auxiliary vertex coordinates. Define HS=12cTc,HB=12bTMBb,MB=MBT>0. H_S=\\tfrac12 c^Tc,\\qquad H_B=\\tfrac12 b^TM_Bb,\\qquad M_B=M_B^T>0. The proposed event receipt records finite changes in these quantities, together with dissipation DD and external work WW: R=ΔHS+ΔHB+D−W. R=\\Delta H_S+\\Delta H_B+D-W. This is a declared accounting test. In the closed, nondissipative case, R=0R=0 reduces to ΔHB=−ΔHS\\Delta H_B=-\\Delta H_S. For a subregion, boundary transfers must also be defined and included. Internal incidence currents redistribute support; they do not by themselves demonstrate conversion into the auxiliary vector. A finite balance is not an infinitesimal law of motion. Even exact closure of this receipt would not identify a unique exchange generator. 2. Symmetry reduces the metric; data identify it If the vertex metric is invariant under the permutation action of S4S_4, then P0=14𝟏𝟏T,P⊥=I−P0,MB=m0P0+m⊥P⊥,m0,m⊥>0. P_0=\\tfrac14\\mathbf1\\mathbf1^T,\\quad P_\\perp=I-P_0,\\quad M_B=m_0P_0+m_\\perp P_\\perp,\\quad m_0,m_\\perp>0. The two parameters are the weights of the uniform and contrast sectors. For closed events, with qr=∥Prb∥2q_r=\\|P_rb\\|^2, each receipt gives m0Δq0+m⊥Δq⊥=−2ΔHS. m_0\\Delta q_0+m_\\perp\\Delta q_\\perp=-2\\Delta H_S. One mixed receipt has rank at most one and cannot uniquely determine both positive weights. Two independent rows can. Sector-isolating events are a convenient sufficient design; a full-rank mixed design is also possible. The symmetry assumption matters. Three equal measurements along an orthonormal contrast basis do not prove isotropy. For example, M=(21/201/220002) M=\\begin{pmatrix}2&1/2&0\\\\1/2&2&0\\\\0&0&2\\end{pmatrix} is positive definite and has three equal diagonal entries, yet gives 5/25/2 along (1,1,0)/2(1,1,0)/\\sqrt2. Either independently justify permutation invariance or test cross terms before treating directional agreement as a complete metric identification. 3. What the revised acquisition specification fixes The supplied version 0.2 supersedes version 0.1 for execution. It defines a fixed orthonormal basis: u0=(1,1,1,1)/2,u1=(1,−1,0,0)/2, u_0=(1,1,1,1)/2,\\quad u_1=(1,-1,0,0)/\\sqrt2, u2=(1,1,−2,0)/6,u3=(1,1,1,−3)/12. u_2=(1,1,-2,0)/\\sqrt6,\\quad u_3=(1,1,1,-3)/\\sqrt{12}. A directional receipt is the treatment-minus-control difference of the pre/post changes in (uiTb)2(u_i^Tb)^2. It is not the squared norm of the difference between treatment and control states. The improved design requires matched initial states and inputs, a fixed support region, the complete four-coordinate auxiliary state, exactly one relevant event, recorded operator order, and immediate response windows. Null controls set the off-axis equivalence floors. Uniform and contrast trials estimate separate positive weights; mixed trials are reserved for checking the fitted balance without refitting. For qualified closed trials, the proposed origin-constrained estimate is m̂i=∑jxjyj∑jxj2,xj=δqi,j,yj=−2δHS,j. \\widehat m_i=\\frac{\\sum_j x_jy_j}{\\sum_jx_j^2},\\qquad x_j=\\delta q_{i,j},\\quad y_j=-2\\delta H_{S,j}. This is undefined without nonzero excitation. If dissipation, external work or boundary transfer has a nonzero attributable contribution, the response must be corrected under an explicit signed accounting convention. The displayed closed-trial formula alone does not perform that correction. Sample maximum null responses are operational tolerances, not confidence or coverage guarantees. Before acquisition, specify sample counts, uncertainty treatment, directional agreement limits and held-out acceptance limits. If the predictor is measured with error, an ordinary slope fit also needs a justified errors-in-variables treatment or an explicit approximation. 4. The analyzer is a slope helper, not a complete scorer Independent synthetic probes confirm that the supplied version 0.2 script computes the advertised slopes from complete numeric pairs. They also show that it prints estimates for deliberately ineligible inputs. Input problem Observed software behavior Required repair before execution Two events, mismatched states, flagged confounding or external receipts The script still computes the same slope. Enforce eligibility and accounting before fitting. Off-axis response in a nominally isolated trial The off-axis receipt is ignored by the selected fit. Apply the frozen null floors to every inactive direction. Duplicate treatment row The last row overwrites the earlier row. Reject duplicate roles and ambiguous pair identifiers. Negative or nonfinite estimate The raw value is printed. Validate finite inputs and classify positivity failures. Missing pair or mixed trial No complete outcome classification is produced. Report exclusions and score the held-out residual explicitly. These are controlled software tests, not experimental observations. The original script is preserved unchanged. Its output must not be presented as a protocol PASS. A qualified scorer must also verify raw-state/receipt consistency, pair metadata, training/held-out separation and the predeclared outcome rules. The uploaded CSV template has consistent 52-column rows; its empty preregistration entries are not acquired data. 5. A conditional reciprocal exchange law On two equally sized state blocks, a supplied constant matrix KK defines JX=(0K−KT0),ẋ=JX∇(HS+HB). J_X=\\begin{pmatrix}0&K\\\\-K^T&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\dot x=J_X\\nabla(H_S+H_B). Thus ċ=Fb\\dot c=Fb, ḃ=−Gc\\dot b=-Gc, with F=KMBF=KM_B and G=KTG=K^T. The identity F=GTMBF=G^TM_B gives exact conservation of the sum of the two quadratic storage functions. This is a constructed finite-dimensional model; conservation does not select KK. If both the coupling and metric have the two-sector form, K=k0P0+k⊥P⊥K=k_0P_0+k_\\perp P_\\perp, the squared sector frequencies are k02m0k_0^2m_0 and k⊥2m⊥k_\\perp^2m_\\perp. Symmetry does not make them equal. A nonnegative frequency is |kr|mr|k_r|\\sqrt{m_r}; a signed generator coefficient is krmrk_r\\sqrt{m_r}. Equal squared frequencies do not fix their relative signs. Bidirectional derivative measurements would identify mr=fr/grm_r=f_r/g_r when gr≠0g_r\\ne0, with the sign convention ḃ=−Gc\\dot b=-Gc kept explicit. The uploaded symbolic examples and the independent controls establish algebraic consistency only. They do not provide recovered UD event coefficients. 6. Parity requires more than an invertible evolution For retained variables q,p∈ℝ3q,p\\in\\mathbb R^3, diagonal tetrahedral symmetry permits the mixed term in H(q,p)=12(a∥q∥2+2χqTp+b∥p∥2). H(q,p)=\\tfrac12\\bigl(a\\|q\\|^2+2\\chi q^Tp+b\\|p\\|^2\\bigr). An independently justified invariance H(q,−p)=H(q,p)H(q,-p)=H(q,p) would force χ=0\\chi=0. Invertibility of a flow, a route orientation or a declaration that pp is odd does not establish that invariance. An action-level argument must additionally specify the time reversal, canonical structure and endpoint conventions needed to induce the stated Hamiltonian parity. The exact finite representation checks give a useful candidate screen: Candidate What is established What it does not establish Oriented K4K_4 gradient/cycle split A commuting involution with two three-dimensional eigenspaces. The sectors are inequivalent S4S_4 representations, so this is not two copies of the same standard representation. Four-coordinate Hodge star Two three-dimensional eigenspaces and compatibility with even permutations. Odd permutations exchange the eigenspaces; it does not commute with all of S4S_4. Swap of two standard representations A commuting involution whose even and odd sectors are both standard. Source selection and invariance of a given action remain separate tests. Paired five-seat B/C standard sectors Each five-seat carrier restricts to 2𝟏⊕V32\\mathbf1\\oplus V_3; its paired standard sectors admit the swap. Full-channel mismatch or isospectrality alone does not settle the projected action test. These are scoped results about specified candidates, not an exclusion of every possible parity. The paired B/C construction is an additional candidate; the earlier two-standard-sector swap already passes the abstract representation test, so uniqueness or an unqualified “first structural pass” is not claimed here. For B/C, the supplied addendum names the remaining projected test P3T5(t)P3=0P_3T_5(t)P_3=0. The dedicated audit is absent from the upload, and no executable projected-action calculation is supplied here. Its result remains open. 7. The next reviewable step Complete the four missing source references listed below and provide the projected B/C action calculation. Turn the version 0.2 written eligibility rules into explicit input rejection, exclusion reporting and held-out scoring. Preserve the present helper as an earlier implementation. Declare the metric symmetry, boundary accounting, uncertainty model and acceptance thresholds before collecting target data. Obtain independent review of that completed protocol, then acquire the matched event receipts. Keep a supplied exchange model distinct from an identified source law. Historical source searches in the uploaded audits are reported as the author’s searches of the named sources. They have not been independently repeated here and do not establish absence from every possible archive. Source completeness and reproduction The supplement preserves 43 available originals: six manifests and 37 referenced files. All 37 available manifest references match their stated SHA-256 values. Four other references are missing; the release is therefore a partial source record, not a complete reproduction of all six original packages. Missing references: UD_FIVE_SEAT_BC_STANDARD_SECTOR_INVOLUTION_AUDIT_v0.1.md UD_FIVE_SEAT_BC_INVOLUTION_STATUS_v0.1.csv UD_PRIMITIVE_LOCAL_SUPPORT_BURDEN_EXCHANGE_GENERATOR_v0.1.md UD_PRIMITIVE_EXCHANGE_GENERATOR_SYMBOLIC_PROBE_v0.1.csv The independent script reconstructs the finite projector and representation calculations, verifies conditional conservation and identifiability counterexamples, and probes the supplied analyzer on synthetic inputs. It does not replay the missing probe file or a physical session. Original source status labels remain historical assertions, with the qualifications above controlling this review’s interpretation. Preserved source documents Protocol and implementation Source Addendum Gate To Burden Exchange Receipt — original Gate To Burden Analyzer — original Gate To Burden Prereg Adversarial Self Review — original Gate To Burden Receipt Analyzer — original Gate To Burden Sector Isolating Prereg — original Gate To Burden Sector Isolating Prereg — original Gate To Burden Sector Isolating Telemetry Schema — original Gate To Burden Telemetry Schema — original Manuscript Addendum Gate Burden Prereg And Involution Screen — original Manuscript Addendum Gate Burden V02 And Five Seat Bc Involution — original Finite algebra and candidate symmetries Source Addendum Event Primitive Parity Polarization — original Source Addendum Local Support Burden Reciprocal Storage Exchange — original Event Primitive Reversibility Orientation Parity Audit — original Manuscript Addendum Event Parity And Primitive Exchange Generator — original Manuscript Addendum Parity Polarization And Gate Burden Receipt — original Manuscript Addendum Primitive Parity And Reciprocal Exchange — original Primitive Event Involution 3Plus3 Screen — original Primitive Exchange Generator Symbolic Validation — original Primitive Five Seat Momentum Parity Audit — original Historical source audits and controls Bidirectional Fg Methodology Validation Result — original Bidirectional Fg Methodology Validation Telemetry — original Bidirectional Fg Methodology Validation — original Development Lane Bidirectional Fg Candida