    "content": "Original source and historical status labels retained. The current review qualifies model definitions, fixed-space memory, topology, storage and reproducibility. SOURCE_ADDENDUM_BURDEN_ANCESTRY_TAGGING_v0.1 Date: 2026-09-18 Status: ADMITTED SOURCE ADDENDUM / PROVENANCE REFINEMENT Physical promotion: 0 Purpose: make inherited burden IinhI_{\\mathrm inh} identifiable without adding a decay, mixing, or inheritance coefficient. 1. Motivation Current aggregate burden continuity is Δρ=BincjB+sB. \\Delta \\rho = B_{\\mathrm inc}j_B+s_B. Aggregate receipts do not identify which portion of later burden descends from a prior parent or source event after mixing. This addendum refines the burden field by ancestry provenance while preserving the aggregate equations exactly. 2. Tagged burden decomposition Let 𝒜\\mathcal A be an append-only set of ancestry/source tags. Define ρi=∑a∈𝒜ρi(a). \\boxed{ \\rho_i = \\sum_{a\\in\\mathcal A} \\rho_i^{(a)}. } Each tag aa has immutable provenance metadata: a=(creation event,creation block/cell,source class). a= ( \\text{creation event}, \\text{creation block/cell}, \\text{source class} ). No numerical parameter is attached to the tag. 3. Tagged continuity Each ancestry component obeys the same typed continuity grammar: Δρ(a)=BincjB(a)+sB(a). \\boxed{ \\Delta\\rho^{(a)} = B_{\\mathrm inc}j_B^{(a)} + s_B^{(a)}. } The tagged currents and sources must sum to the aggregate objects: jB=∑ajB(a), \\boxed{ j_B = \\sum_a j_B^{(a)}, } sB=∑asB(a). \\boxed{ s_B = \\sum_a s_B^{(a)}. } Therefore ∑aΔρ(a)=Binc∑ajB(a)+∑asB(a)=BincjB+sB. \\sum_a \\Delta\\rho^{(a)} = B_{\\mathrm inc} \\sum_a j_B^{(a)} + \\sum_a s_B^{(a)} = B_{\\mathrm inc}j_B+s_B. So the addendum is exactly aggregate-compatible. AUTO_LOCK ANCESTRY_TAGGED_CONTINUITY_SUMS_EXACTLY_TO_AGGREGATE_BURDEN_CONTINUITY_v0.1 4. No spontaneous retagging Transport and redistribution preserve ancestry labels. A burden element may change location but not provenance. New positive burden creation