    "content": "Exact local spectra and transported-load observables, with explicit limits on memory, capacity and event selection. Original sources and independent replay included. Tagged Load, Response Capacity and Pachner Spectral Change Supporting mathematical review · 18 September 2026 The new developments make two parts of UD more explicit: how a recorded load redistributes on a finite graph, and how the support operator changes when a local triangulation is replaced. The strongest results are exact matrix identities, conservation and dissipation statements, and a demand-weighted response ratio. They do not yet select when a retriangulation occurs, how a state crosses that event, or how much load a physical carrier can store. This review incorporates the completed 71-file batch and two earlier files referenced by its manifests. It distinguishes the current definitions from earlier proposals retained in the source record. Papers I and II remain frozen; this is a supporting development note. Reading route: Theorem paper → previous persistence review → the present note → preserved sources and reproduction package. 1. Two state spaces, two evolution laws Let KK be a finite oriented tetrahedral simplicial complex, with oriented boundary matrices Bk:Ck→Ck−1B_k:C_k\\to C_{k-1}. Its real chain state is c∈⨁k=03Ckc\\in\\bigoplus_{k=0}^3 C_k. The adjacent-degree skew matrix 𝒜K\\mathcal A_K has upper blocks BkB_k and lower blocks −Bk⊤-B_k^\\top. The standard identities B1B2=B2B3=0,𝒜K⊤=−𝒜K B_1B_2=B_2B_3=0,\\qquad \\mathcal A_K^\\top=-\\mathcal A_K give conservation of the Euclidean chain norm under ċ=𝒜Kc\\dot c=\\mathcal A_Kc. A separate vertex field bb, called burden in the source, records a transported load. With a declared diagonal gate matrix HH, 0≼H≼I0\\preceq H\\preceq I, the Q162 model is jB=−14HB1⊤b,ḃ=−RBb+sB,RB=14B1HB1⊤. j_B=-\\tfrac14 HB_1^\\top b,\\qquad \\dot b=-R_Bb+s_B,\\qquad R_B=\\tfrac14 B_1HB_1^\\top. Here RBR_B is symmetric positive semidefinite and 𝟏⊤RB=0\\mathbf1^\\top R_B=0. Closed, source-free diffusion conserves total load. For a fixed connected open-edge graph it relaxes to the mean. Connectivity at isolated times alone is insufficient for that asymptotic conclusion under changing gates. These are distinct models: the chain evolution is norm-preserving, while the load evolution is dissipative. Their parameters are internal evolution coordinates. Neither equation identifies a physical time or a measured energy. 2. Provenance resolves inherited load when tags are supplied Write b=∑ab(a)b=\\sum_a b^{(a)}, where each tag records a source event. For a fixed graph and the same prescribed gate history, every component satisfies ḃ(a)=−RBb(a)+sB(a). \\dot b^{(a)}=-R_Bb^{(a)}+s_B^{(a)}. Summing recovers the aggregate equation. For a cell DD with birth event tDt_D, one declared inherited-load convention is ID=∑a:ta<tD∑i∈Dbi(a). I_D=\\sum_{a:t_a<t_D}\\sum_{i\\in D}b_i^{(a)}. This quantity is exactly computable from the tagged state. Tags add information; they cannot recover an unrecorded ancestry retrospectively from aggregate totals. The optional restriction to tags present at birth must be specified because it changes the observable. On a fixed interval with constant RBR_B, each component has the usual matrix-exponential solution with a source integral. Predicting it requires the initial tagged field, gates and source terms. Linearity applies with a shared prescribed operator; independently changing the gates for each component would not justify superposition. A daughter sharing three old vertices inherits a restriction of the tagged field to those vertices, assuming a new apex initially carries no old tag. This local trace overlaps the parent’s stock. Summing such traces over cells double-counts shared vertices unless an ownership partition is supplied. 3. Clock normalization is part of the model On K4K_4, B1B1⊤=4P⊥B_1B_1^\\top=4P_\\perp. The source’s two fixed normalizations produce rates 11 and 4/34/3 on the zero