iagnostic gives e−λ(s−s0)e^{-\\lambda(s-s_0)}; these should not be interchanged. Setting M=0M=0 for zero reference contrast is a declared convention. The monotonicity statement needs its full domain. A global mean-removing projector works for time-varying graph Laplacians on a fixed vertex set. A projector that changes as components split contributes additional terms. A sub-block exchanging load with its surroundings need not have decreasing contrast. On a three-vertex path with ḃ=−Lb\\dot b=-Lb and b=(4,1,0)⊤b=(4,1,0)^\\top, the squared contrast within the last two vertices has derivative +1+1, although global squared contrast decreases. Likewise, births, changing dimensions, sinks and a changing tag cohort require explicit interval and transfer rules. An old cohort with normalized power 0.10.1 gains aggregate value 0.550.55 if a new tag with equal reference power and value 11 is appended. That is consistent with the definition, but prevents a claim of monotone aggregate memory across births. Tagging new sources does not remove boundary forcing on old tags. Inherited stock and retained contrast answer different questions. A uniform tagged field may have positive inherited stock and zero contrast memory. 5. Response capacity is a defined, testable scalar For a fixed field and declared graph, let qe=(B1⊤b)e2q_e=(B_1^\\top b)_e^2. The new response-capacity definition is V=∑eheqe∑eqe,∑eqe>0. V=\\frac{\\sum_e h_eq_e}{\\sum_e q_e},\\qquad \\sum_e q_e>0. It compares the instantaneous relaxation quadratic form with the all-open form on the same graph and state. Thus 0≤V≤10\\le V\\le1; positive common clock scaling cancels; rescaling the field or adding a constant leaves the ratio unchanged. Opening a gate cannot decrease VV while the field and denominator remain fixed. Comparing later trajectories does not satisfy that condition. The convention V=1V=1 at zero demand is explicit, not a continuous-extension theorem. It means there is no redistribution requirement in this model; it does not establish storage tolerance, survival or physical viability. For b=(3,1,−1,−3)⊤b=(3,1,-1,-3)^\\top on K4K_4, the six demands are (4,16,36,4,16,4)(4,16,36,4,16,4). Opening edges 01,02,12,2301,02,12,23 gives V=28/80=7/20V=28/80=7/20, whereas the unweighted open-edge fraction is 2/32/3. The distinction is substantive. Equality with an unweighted fraction requires equal positive demands over the same edge set; a boundary-only gate count is not generally a whole-graph ratio. The mathematical properties are exact consequences of the definition. Calling this particular ratio the historical UD coordinate VV is a supplied semantic choice, not a proof that generic monotonicity conditions select a unique scalar. The earlier product-versus-minimum counterexample remains valid for that broader question. 6. Aggregation is exact; reduction of dynamics is a separate problem Allocate each global edge’s demand to its incident cells with nonnegative ownership weights summing to one. Equal shares we,τ=1/n3(e)w_{e,\\tau}=1/n_3(e) are one such choice. Set Dτ=∑e⊂τwe,τqe,Aτ=∑e⊂τwe,τheqe. D_\\tau=\\sum_{e\\subset\\tau}w_{e,\\tau}q_e,\\qquad A_\\tau=\\sum_{e\\subset\\tau}w_{e,\\tau}h_eq_e. For nonzero global demand, Vglobal=∑τDτVτ∑τDτ. V_{\\mathrm{global}}= \\frac{\\sum_\\tau D_\\tau V_\\tau}{\\sum_\\tau D_\\tau}. The proof is the partition-of-unity identity on every edge. It establishes exact aggregation of a recorded observable, not a closed evolution equation for cell averages or invariance under changing the complex. It also requires every modeled edge to have an owner. The supplied four-tetrahedron report contains 12 global and 30 cell summaries. Their ratios and owned-demand sums are consistent within rounding. The original initial tagged vectors and executable simulation are absent, so those summaries do not permit an independent replay of the reported trajectory or its stated maximum conservation error. The supplement includes a separate, fully specified four-cell control verifying conservation and aggregation; it is not represented as the original run or as experimental evidence. 7. Storage and obstruction remain separate constitutive questions For nonnegative tagged load, B=𝟏⊤bB=\\mathbf1^\\top b and 0≤I≤B0\\le I\\le B. The inherited fraction ι=I/B\\iota=I/B is scale-free when B>0B>0, with a declared zero-stock convention. A unit-invariant quantity depending only on (B,V,M,I)(B,V,M,I) cannot distinguish absolute load magnitude under (B,I)↦(αB,αI)(B,I)\\mapsto(\\alpha B,\\alpha I) without another scale. An independently specified reference B⋆B_\\star permits β=B/B⋆\\beta=B/B_\\star. That scale still does not select an obstruction function. On nonnegative normalized coordinates z=(β,1−V,M,ι)z=(\\beta,1-V,M,\\iota), the functions ∑izi\\sum_i z_i, ∑ilog(1+zi)\\sum_i\\log(1+z_i), and ∏i(1+zi)−1\\prod_i(1+z_i)-1 satisfy null and monotonicity conditions while differing numerically. A unit multiplier on an already defined obstruction channel does not choose its internal formula. Two further qualifications matter. Monotonicity in BB at fixed II does not automatically become monotonicity in β\\beta at fixed ι\\iota; changing coordinates changes what is held constant. A positive-definite quadratic metric also need not yield a coordinatewise monotone obstruction on the positive orthant. For example, the matrix with diagonal entries 11 and off-diagonal entries −3/4-3/4 is positive definite, but its quadratic form has a negative first partial derivative at (0,1)(0,1). For fixed gates, the transformation b↦b+k𝟏b\\mapsto b+k\\mathbf1 leaves currents and contrasts unchanged while increasing stock by kNkN. If the admissible set permits these positive shifts, it has no universal finite stock ceiling. This is a statement across admissible initial states, not unbounded growth along a closed diffusion trajectory, whose total stock is conserved. 8. Quadratic storage provides a representation, not a capacity law Choose the Euclidean storage function