rlevel−fR,rmeter; R_{L,r}=Q_{L,r}^{\\mathrm level}-f_{L,r}^{\\mathrm meter}, \\qquad R_{R,r}=Q_{R,r}^{\\mathrm level}-f_{R,r}^{\\mathrm meter}; G14flow,G14level,R14. G_{14}^{\\mathrm flow}, \\qquad G_{14}^{\\mathrm level}, \\qquad R_{14}. It also checks the exact identity R14=(RL,1−RL,0)−(RR,1−RR,0)4. R_{14} = \\frac{(R_{L,1}-R_{L,0})-(R_{R,1}-R_{R,0})}{4}. 6. Metrology gate This package supports two source-governed uncertainty routes. Route H — hard maximum-error bound The calibration manifest must supply authenticated absolute bounds for: each tank area BAiB_{A_i}; each per-sample level channel BhiB_{h_i}; measured flow BfL,BfRB_{f_L},B_{f_R}; timing bound if material, otherwise an authenticated timing_negligible=true receipt. The scorer propagates the frozen hard-bound theorem. Route C — standard covariance The calibration manifest must supply: a complete 10×1010\\times10 covariance matrix for z=(A1,A2,A3,A4,Δm1,Δm2,Δm3,Δm4,ΔfL,ΔfR), z=(A_1,A_2,A_3,A_4,\\Delta m_1,\\Delta m_2,\\Delta m_3,\\Delta m_4,\\Delta f_L,\\Delta f_R), its source/calculation receipt; a pretarget coverage factor kcovk_{\\mathrm cov}. The scorer evaluates u2(R14)≈JRΣzJRT. u^2(R_{14})\\approx J_R\\Sigma_zJ_R^T. 7. No default uncertainty The distributed calibration template deliberately contains no installed-instrument accuracy. The scorer returns: SOURCE_BLOCKED if any required uncertainty slot is null, absent, non-finite, or lacks the declared source receipt identity. No generic WIKA, electromagnetic-flowmeter, NI-DAQ, or catalog tolerance is inserted. 8. Pre-score freeze requirement Before outcome scoring: preserve the raw data file unchanged; populate the run manifest from the source-declared protocol; populate the calibration manifest from authenticated source receipts; run freeze_receipts.py; preserve the resulting PRE_SCORE_FREEZE.json. score_primary.py and score_independent.py refuse execution unless: the raw data hash matches; the run-manifest hash matches; the calibration-manifest hash matches; the package scientific-source hash matches; every required source slot is closed. 9. Verdicts For hard-bound route: EXECUTION_PASS iff |R14| <= B_R14 EXECUTION_FAIL iff |R14| > B_R14 For covariance route: EXECUTION_PASS iff |R14| <= k_cov*u(R14) EXECUTION_FAIL iff |R14| > k_cov*u(R14) Other dispositions: SOURCE_BLOCKED DATA_BLOCKED INTEGRITY_FAIL No alternative metric may replace the primary verdict. 10. Physical claim boundary A PASS would establish a scoped same-apparatus agreement between: directly measured branch-flow contrast, and independently level-derived hydraulic branch contrast, within a pretarget source-authored uncertainty band. It would not establish fundamental physical identity between the UD edge carrier and an established field. PHYSICAL_PROMOTION := 0"
