rm flow}. Why it is blocked today Public sources do not provide: Lehigh tank level→volume geometry; a run-specific all-nonpump-flow-isolated valve receipt; tank-level sensor metrology; delivered pump-flow provenance. The templates in this release intentionally leave those fields empty. No generic quadruple-tank geometry is permitted. Physical promotion: 0. manuscript/UD_JOP_v2.40_LEHIGH_TANK_SIDE_COMPARATOR_ADDENDUM_v0.1.mdJOP v2.40 Addendum — Prospective Lehigh Independent Tank-Side Comparator v0.1 A prospective Lehigh/Bitlismen same-apparatus comparator is preregistered for the already derived branch-contrast source component G14,flow=Δq1−Δq24. G_{14,\\mathrm flow} = \\frac{\\Delta q_1-\\Delta q_2}{4}. The independent target is obtained from tank storage rates during a source-declared hydraulic fill-isolation configuration. For general source-authored tank geometry Vi(hi)V_i(h_i), V̇i=dVidhiḣi. \\dot V_i = \\frac{dV_i}{dh_i}\\dot h_i. When all non-pump outlet and intertank transfer paths are physically closed, q1tank=V̇1+V̇4,q2tank=V̇2+V̇3. q_1^{\\mathrm tank}=\\dot V_1+\\dot V_4, \\qquad q_2^{\\mathrm tank}=\\dot V_2+\\dot V_3. The independent target is G14,tank=Δq1tank−Δq2tank4, G_{14,\\mathrm tank} = \\frac{\\Delta q_1^{\\mathrm tank}-\\Delta q_2^{\\mathrm tank}}{4}, with residual R14(Lehigh)=G14,tank−G14,flow. R_{14}^{(\\mathrm Lehigh)} = G_{14,\\mathrm tank}-G_{14,\\mathrm flow}. For constant-area tanks this reduces to storage rates AiḣiA_i\\dot h_i, but no constant-area, cylindrical, Johansson, Córdoba, or numerical-QTP geometry is assumed. The public Bitlismen/Lehigh sources support measured tank levels and controllable hydraulic paths but do not currently publish the Lehigh tank level-to-volume geometry or a run-specific isolation receipt. The comparator is therefore frozen prospectively but remains source-blocked for execution. Physical promotion remains zero. protocol/UD_LEHIGH_INDEPENDENT_TANK_SIDE_COMPARATOR_PREREG_v0.1.mdUD Lehigh Independent Tank-Side Comparator Preregistration v0.1 Generated: 2026-09-09T02:18:36.121136+00:00 Status: PRETARGET_FROZEN / SOURCE_GEOMETRY_AND_ISOLATION_RECEIPTS_PENDING Claim class: PROSPECTIVE_INDEPENDENT_PHYSICAL_COMPARATOR Physical promotion: 0 0. Objective Create a genuinely independent Lehigh/Bitlismen tank-side comparator for the already frozen delivered-flow branch contrast Cbr(LEHIGH)=Δq1−Δq2, C_{\\mathrm br}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = \\Delta q_1-\\Delta q_2, G14,flow(LEHIGH)=Δq1−Δq24. G_{14,\\mathrm flow}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = \\frac{\\Delta q_1-\\Delta q_2}{4}. The target channel must be derived from tank-level/geometry measurements and a source-declared hydraulic isolation configuration, not from the pump command→flow calibration being tested. This comparator is prospective. Existing InTaSet tank outcomes are not used to select or calibrate it. 1. Source-authored hardware facts already available The Lehigh/Bitlismen source family supports: four tank-level pressure measurements; two independently controlled pumps; Pump 1 support on Tanks 1 and 4; Pump 2 support on Tanks 2 and 3; manual valves on tank outlet paths; solenoid control of pump inlet flow; configurable hydraulic couplings using interchangeable tube diameters. The exact 14/2314/23 source law is independent of the unknown pump split fractions. These source facts are sufficient to define a prospective fill-isolation experiment. They are not sufficient to execute it because the public package does not currently provide: source-authored tank level→volume geometry; a Lehigh run-specific valve/isolation configuration receipt; installed level-sensor metrology; authenticated delivered pump-flow telemetry/calibration. 2. Geometry carrier — no cylindrical assumption For each tank i∈{1,2,3,4}i\\in\\{1,2,3,4\\}, require a source-authored volume law Vi=Vi(hi) V_i=V_i(h_i) on the experimental level domain. Define the differential storage capacity Ki(hi):=dVidhi. \\boxed{ K_i(h_i):=\\frac{dV_i}{dh_i}. } Then the level-derived storage-rate channel is V̇i=Ki(hi)ḣi. \\boxed{ \\dot V_i = K_i(h_i)\\dot h_i. } This formulation does not assume that the tanks are cylindrical or share equal cross-sectional areas. Constant-area specialization Only if a source geometry receipt states that the relevant tank region has constant area AiA_i, Vi(hi)=Aihi+Vi,0, V_i(h_i)=A_i h_i+V_{i,0}, then Ki(hi)=Ai \\boxed{ K_i(h_i)=A_i } and V̇i=Aiḣi. \\dot V_i=A_i\\dot h_i. No Córdoba tank areas, Johansson parameters, numerical-QTP areas, photograph scaling, or generic Bitlismen dimensions may populate this source slot. 3. Frozen hydraulic isolation configuration A scored run must use a source-declared configuration in which all non-pump tank flows entering the storage balance are either: A. physically closed / isolated, or B. independently measured and included as predeclared correction channels. The preferred v0.1 comparator is Mode A: physical isolation. Mode A — fill isolation Before target acquisition, the source/operator receipt must identify the physical valve state showing that, during each scored fill window: pump inlet path is enabled as declared; tank outlet-to-reservoir paths are closed; upper-to-lower/intertank gravity-transfer paths are closed; alternate/bypass outlet paths are closed; no unmeasured drain, overflow, or recirculation path is active. Under this declared configuration: q1,rtank=V̇1,r+V̇4,r, \\boxed{ q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = \\dot V_{1,r}+\\dot V_{4,r}, } q2,rtank=V̇2,r+V̇3,r. \\boxed{ q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = \\dot V_{2,r}+\\dot V_{3,r}. } The pump split fractions inside each branch are irrelevant because the two tank storage rates are summed. Mode B — corrected mass balance Mode B is not executable in v0.1. If the physical rig cannot isolate the non-pump flows, every remaining inflow/outflow term must be independently measured or source-modeled in a separately versioned protocol before scoring. No generic Torricelli coefficient, outlet-orifice area, discharge coefficient, or numerical-model parameter may be inserted into v0.1. 4. Two-state fresh experiment Use two source-declared, non-overlapping fill windows: r∈{0,1}. r\\in\\{0,1\\}. The pump source channel provides independently authenticated delivered-flow states q1,0flow,q1,1flow, q_{1,0}^{\\mathrm flow},\\quad q_{1,1}^{\\mathrm flow}, q2,0flow,q2,1flow. q_{2,0}^{\\mathrm flow},\\quad q_{2,1}^{\\mathrm flow}. The tank-side channel is derived independently from level and geometry. For general geometry, define the window-average tank storage rate V̇‾i,r=1|Wr|∑n∈WrKi(hi,n)ḣi,n, \\bar{\\dot V}_{i,r} = \\frac1{|W_r|} \\sum_{n\\in W_r} K_i(h_{i,n})\\dot h_{i,n}, using the frozen level-derivative estimator and source geometry law. Then q1,rtank=V̇‾1,r+V̇‾4,r, q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = \\bar{\\dot V}_{1,r} + \\bar{\\dot V}_{4,r}, q2,rtank=V̇‾2,r+V̇‾3,r. q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = \\bar{\\dot V}_{2,r} + \\bar{\\dot V}_{3,r}. Constant-area linear-fill specialization If geometry is constant-area and each source-declared fill window is admitted as linear, mi,r=dhidt|Wr, m_{i,r} = \\frac{d h_i}{dt}\\Big|_{W_r}, then q1,rtank=A1m1,r+A4m4,r, \\boxed{ q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = A_1m_{1,r}+A_4m_{4,r}, } q2,rtank=A2m2,r+A3m3,r. \\boxed{ q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm tank} = A_2m_{2,r}+A_3m_{3,r}. } This specialization is closest to the already frozen Córdoba comparator but remains a distinct Lehigh experimental object with independently sourced geometry and uncertainty. 5. Independent Lehigh target Define Δq1tank=q1,1tank−q1,0tank, \\Delta q_1^{\\mathrm tank} = q_{1,1}^{\\mathrm tank}-q_{1,0}^{\\mathrm tank}, Δq2tank=q2,1tank−q2,0tank. \\Delta q_2^{\\mathrm tank} = q_{2,1}^{\\mathrm tank}-q_{2,0}^{\\mathrm tank}. The tank-side target is G14,tank(LEHIGH)=Δq1tank−Δq2tank4. \\boxed{ G_{14,\\mathrm tank}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = \\frac{ \\Delta q_1^{\\mathrm tank} - \\Delta q_2^{\\mathrm tank} }{4}. } The independently sourced pump-flow prediction is G14,flow(LEHIGH)=Δq1flow−Δq2flow4. \\boxed{ G_{14,\\mathrm flow}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = \\frac{ \\Delta q_1^{\\mathrm flow} - \\Delta q_2^{\\mathrm flow} }{4}. } Primary physical residual: R14(LEHIGH)=G14,tank(LEHIGH)−G14,flow(LEHIGH). \\boxed{ R_{14}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = G_{14,\\mathrm tank}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} - G_{14,\\mathrm flow}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})}. } This is not the identity G14=−G23G_{14}=-G_{23} computed twice from the same flow source. It compares pump-side delivered-flow provenance with an independent tank storage-rate measurement path. 6. Exact branch-closure decomposition At state rr, define typed branch closure receipts B1,r=q1,rtank−q1,rflow, B_{1,r} = q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm tank} - q_{1,r}^{\\mathrm flow}, B2,r=q2,rtank−q2,rflow. B_{2,r} = q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm tank} - q_{2,r}^{\\mathrm flow}. Then exactly R14(LEHIGH)=(B1,1−B1,0)−(B2,1−B2,0)4. \\boxed{ R_{14}^{(\\mathrm{LEHIGH})} = \\frac{ (B_{1,1}-B_{1,0}) - (B_{2,1}-B_{2,0}) }{4}. } This decomposition is independent of the internal pump split parameters. 7. Pretarget window rule Before opening the fresh target channel, freeze: run ID; configuration ID; source geometry receipt; valve/isolation state; pump-flow calibration/direct-flow receipt; pump state 0 and state 1; transient exclusion interval; level-fit duration; derivative/slope estimator; uncertainty model and PASS band. No window may move after inspecting R14R_{14}. 8. Isolation qualification gate The operator/source must provide an explicit pretarget isolation receipt. Required fields: pump1_to_tanks_1_4 := confirmed pump2_to_tanks_2_3 := confirmed tank_outlet_to_reservoir_paths := CLOSED intertank_gravity_transfer_paths := CLOSED alternate_upper_outlet_paths := CLOSED unmeasured_bypass_paths := NONE / CLOSED overflow_possible_in_fit_windows := FALSE If a physical path cannot be classified from the source/operator configuration: SOURCE_BLOCKED_CONFIGURATION A photograph alone is not sufficient unless the source operator identifies the valve/path state. A pre-run leak test may be added only after its sensor-derived threshold is frozen. No zero-leak claim is inferred from command state alone. 9. Geometry qualification gate The geometry receipt must provide one of: G1 — full level→volume functions Vi(h) V_i(h) with domain and uncertainty; G2 — level→storage-capacity functions Ki(h)=dVi/dh K_i(h)=dV_i/dh with domain and uncertainty; G3 — constant tank areas Ai A_i with valid level interval and uncertainty. Missing geometry: SOURCE_BLOCKED_GEOMETRY Generic product photographs, Córdoba geometry, Johansson geometry, or inverse fitting from tank-response outcomes are prohibited. 10. Metrology gate The numerical PASS band must be frozen from authenticated source uncertainty for: delivered pump-flow measurement/calibration; each tank level channel; level→volume geometry; timing/derivative estimation if material; any declared residual leak bound if isolation is imperfect. No numerical tolerance is defined in v0.1. Until these receipts arrive: NUMERIC_PASS_THRESHOLD := SOURCE_BLOCKED 11. Allowed verdicts SOURCE_BLOCKED_GEOMETRY SOURCE_BLOCKED_CONFIGURATION SOURCE_BLOCKED_PUMP_FLOW SOURCE_BLOCKED_METROLOGY DATA_BLOCKED EXECUTION_PASS EXECUTION_FAIL A blocked result is not converted to a candidate PASS. 12. Cross-platform relationship If this Lehigh comparator is later executed under its frozen uncertainty gate, it becomes the missing second physical comparator required by the existing cross-platform status ladder. Only if: CORDOBA comparator := EXECUTION_PASS LEHIGH comparator := EXECUTION_PASS both source-law lanes := authenticated may the cross-platform reporter assign: DUAL_PHYSICAL_COMPARATOR_REPLICATION_PASS within the scoped QTP experiment. The two comparator residuals are not pooled or normalized against one another. 13. Current source status At freeze time: LEHIGH_LEVEL_CHANNELS := SOURCE_CONFIRMED LEHIGH_MANUAL_OUTLET_VALVES := SOURCE_CONFIRMED_FAMILY LEHIGH_PUMP_INLET_SOLENOIDS := SOURCE_CONFIRMED_FAMILY LEHIGH_CONFIGURABLE_COUPLING_TUBES := SOURCE_CONFIRMED_FAMILY LEHIGH_COUPLING_TUBE_