red physical active amplitude is ar=qr2. a_r=q_r^2. Because qr=2φr, q_r=\\sqrt2\\,\\varphi_r, the Euclidean-active modal masses are Ma=2C1ϕ02 \\boxed{ M_a = 2C_1\\phi_0^2 } Mb=2C3ϕ02 \\boxed{ M_b = 2C_3\\phi_0^2 } Mc=2ϕ02C1C3(C1+C3)C12+C32. \\boxed{ M_c = 2\\phi_0^2 \\frac{ C_1C_3(C_1+C_3) }{ C_1^2+C_3^2 }. } The factor-of-two relation between source canonical coordinates and Euclidean-active coordinates is explicit provenance, not a fit. 5. Action-scale family For a harmonic normal mode, 𝒜r=Mrωr. \\mathcal A_r = M_r\\omega_r. Define the common published linear stiffness object GJRM:=EJeffϕ02+12Lshunt. \\boxed{ G_{\\mathrm JRM} := \\frac{E_J^{\\mathrm eff}}{\\phi_0^2} + \\frac{1}{2L_{\\mathrm shunt}}. } Then C1=GJRMωa2, C_1 = \\frac{G_{\\mathrm JRM}}{\\omega_a^2}, C3=GJRMωb2. C_3 = \\frac{G_{\\mathrm JRM}}{\\omega_b^2}. Therefore Ma=2ϕ02GJRMωa2 \\boxed{ M_a = \\frac{ 2\\phi_0^2G_{\\mathrm JRM} }{ \\omega_a^2 } } Mb=2ϕ02GJRMωb2 \\boxed{ M_b = \\frac{ 2\\phi_0^2G_{\\mathrm JRM} }{ \\omega_b^2 } } and 𝒜a=2ϕ02GJRMωa \\boxed{ \\mathcal A_a = \\frac{ 2\\phi_0^2G_{\\mathrm JRM} }{ \\omega_a } } 𝒜b=2ϕ02GJRMωb. \\boxed{ \\mathcal A_b = \\frac{ 2\\phi_0^2G_{\\mathrm JRM} }{ \\omega_b }. } Thus all absolute modal masses/action scales remain a one-parameter family controlled by GJRMG_{\\mathrm JRM}. 6. Exact source-complete ratios The unknown common stiffness cancels. Hence C3C1=(ωaωb)2 \\boxed{ \\frac{C_3}{C_1} = \\left( \\frac{\\omega_a}{\\omega_b} \\right)^2 } MaMb=(ωbωa)2 \\boxed{ \\frac{M_a}{M_b} = \\left( \\frac{\\omega_b}{\\omega_a} \\right)^2 } and 𝒜a𝒜b=ωbωa. \\boxed{ \\frac{\\mathcal A_a}{\\mathcal A_b} = \\frac{\\omega_b}{\\omega_a}. } Using only the published experimental frequencies: C3C1=2.34932783265845 \\boxed{ \\frac{C_3}{C_1} = 2.34932783265845 } MaMb=0.425653664039054 \\boxed{ \\frac{M_a}{M_b} = 0.425653664039054 } 𝒜a𝒜b=0.652421385332405. \\boxed{ \\frac{\\mathcal A_a}{\\mathcal A_b} = 0.652421385332405. } These are target-independent empirical/model-derived receipts. 7. Multimode single-action-scale no-go The current single-K4K_4 Hodge theorem gives one intensive action scale SnativeaΔϕ̃=𝒜02 \\frac{ S_{\\mathrm native} }{ a\\,\\Delta\\widetilde\\phi } = \\frac{\\mathcal A_0}{2} independent of active-state amplitude and active direction inside that carrier. Suppose both physical JRM modes aa and bb are mapped isometrically to that same native active carrier with one shared physical action unit. Then it is necessary that 𝒜a=𝒜b. \\mathcal A_a=\\mathcal A_b. But the source-complete ratio is 𝒜a𝒜b=0.652421385332405≠1. \\frac{\\mathcal A_a}{\\mathcal A_b} = 0.652421385332405 \\ne1. Therefore: the Chien a and b modes cannot both realize one universal 𝒜0 under the direct isometric node-phase intertwiner. \\boxed{ \\text{the Chien \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) modes cannot both realize one universal } \\mathcal A_0 \\text{ under the direct isometric node-phase intertwiner.} } Classification: LOCKED_NO_GO_WITHIN_PUBLISHED_LINEAR_MODEL_AND_DECLARED_ISOMETRIC_MAP. This does not falsify QPB1 as a natural-law claim. It falsifies this particular two-mode physical realization of a single UD action scale. A repair would require an independently sourced, non-isometric mode metric/intertwiner. Such a repair cannot be chosen after seeing the QPB1 target. 8. Why the absolute Class-A QPB1 score remains blocked The paper supplies approximate/design information such as: target junction current around 2μA2\\,\\mu{\\mathrm A}; shunt inductance around 75pH75\\,{\\mathrm pH}; β≈4.5\\beta\\approx4.5 as close to experimental conditions. But the measured a,ba,b frequencies are taken at a Kerr-minimizing operating point for which the source does not provide one exact numerical receipt containing all of: α,ϑ,Ic,Lshunt \\alpha, \\quad \\vartheta, \\quad I_c, \\quad L_{\\mathrm shunt} at that same measured point. Therefore GJRMG_{\\mathrm JRM} is not numerically source-closed. Using approximate design values to choose GJRMG_{\\mathrm JRM} would create an uncontrolled scale estimate. Backsolving GJRMG_{\\mathrm JRM} from QPB1 is forbidden. Thus: ηa,ηb absolute values remain OPEN. \\boxed{ \\eta_a,\\eta_b \\text{ absolute values remain OPEN.} } 9. Mode cc The source gives Mc=2ϕ02C1C3(C1+C3)C12+C32. M_c = 2\\phi_0^2 \\frac{ C_1C_3(C_1+C_3) }{ C_1^2+C_3^2 }. Using the source-complete capacitance ratio, this mass is known up to the same single common scale C1C_1 or GJRMG_{\\mathrm JRM}. However the audited paper does not provide a scoreable fcf_c resonance at the selected operating point. Therefore: MODE_C_ACTION_SCORE_SOURCE_BLOCKED. No pump sum/difference frequency is silently substituted for the natural resonance ωc\\omega_c. 10. Final status EXACT / DERIVED modal kinetic masses in source coordinates; Euclidean-active mass map; C3/C1C_3/C_1; Ma/MbM_a/M_b; 𝒜a/𝒜b\\mathcal A_a/\\mathcal A_b. NO-GO A single universal action scale across both measured a,ba,b modes under the direct isometric map. OPEN Absolute 𝒜a,𝒜b,ηa,ηb\\mathcal A_a,\\mathcal A_b,\\eta_a,\\eta_b due to one unresolved source scale GJRMG_{\\mathrm JRM}. AUTO_FREEZE no QPB1 backsolve; no mode cherry-picking; no pump frequency substituted for ωc\\omega_c; no post-result mode-dependent normalization repair. Physical promotion remains 00. UD_KHEZRI2021_GENERALIZED_ACTION_MODE_INTERTWINER_v0.1.mdUD_KHEZRI2021_GENERALIZED_ACTION_MODE_INTERTWINER_v0.1 Date: 2026-09-13 Source: M. Khezri et al., npj Quantum Information 7, 36 (2021), DOI 10.1038/s41534-021-00371-9 Class: A1_PREDATING_AUXILIARY Status: DERIVED_GENERAL_ACTION_MODE_INTERTWINER__SOURCE_MASS_METRICS_NUMERICALLY_CLOSED__BIAS_SPECIFIC_ACTION_SCORE_OPEN Physical promotion: 0 1. Source Hamiltonian The experimental four-junction capacitively shunted flux qubit has two node phases φ=(φ1,φ2)𝖳 \\varphi=(\\varphi_1,\\varphi_2)^\\mathsf T and capacitance matrix C=(Csh+(2α+1)Cz−Cz−Cz2Cz). \\boxed{ C = \\begin{pmatrix} C_{\\mathrm sh}+(2\\alpha+1)C_z & -C_z\\\\ -C_z & 2C_z \\end{pmatrix}. } The physical phase kinetic metric is