    "content": "Corrects the source schedule, superseding the earlier late-drift conclusion. Joint cluster admission remains a source-regime candidate, with the historical count already known before testing. Governed release package · 0.1Source-Schedule Repair and Joint Cluster AdmissionCorrects the source schedule, superseding the earlier late-drift conclusion. Joint cluster admission remains a source-regime candidate, with the historical count already known before testing.StatusSCHEDULE REPAIRED / SCOPED SIMULATIONPhysical promotion0Package files14Hash manifestVerified · 13 filesDownload immutable release ZIP ↓Package compositionpackage root14Show all 14 preserved pathsSOURCE_v07_genesis_sim_v1.pyUD_FOURTH_CUMULANT_SOURCE_SCHEDULE_REPAIR_v0.1.mdUD_JOINT_CLUSTER_HELDOUT_v0.1.jsonUD_JOINT_CLUSTER_RULE_FREEZE_v0.1.jsonUD_JOINT_SPATIOTEMPORAL_CLUSTER_ADMISSION_v0.1.mdUD_KAPPA4_EFFECT_SIZE_v0.1.jsonUD_KAPPA4_JOINT_CLUSTER_MANIFEST_v0.1.jsonUD_KAPPA4_JOINT_CLUSTER_REPRODUCER_v0.1.pyUD_KAPPA4_JOINT_CLUSTER_STATUS_v0.1.jsonUD_KAPPA4_ORACLE_AUTONOMOUS_COMPARISON_v0.1.jsonUD_MANUSCRIPT_ADDENDUM_KAPPA4_JOINT_CLUSTER_v0.1.mdUD_PHI_AUTONOMOUS_CLOSURE_SOURCE_SCHEDULE_REPAIR_v0.2.mdUD_SOURCE_LOCAL_CUMULANT_SHAPE_v0.1.jsonUD_SOURCE_SCHEDULE_GAUSSIAN_HELDOUT_v0.1.jsonUD_FOURTH_CUMULANT_SOURCE_SCHEDULE_REPAIR_v0.1.mdUD_FOURTH_CUMULANT_SOURCE_SCHEDULE_REPAIR_v0.1 Date: 2026-09-13 Type: VERSION REPAIR / CUMULANT AUDIT Status: SOURCE_SCHEDULE_REPAIR_PASS__LOCAL_KAPPA4_NOT_LOAD_BEARING__NONLOCAL_KAPPA4_OPEN Physical promotion: 0 1. Mandatory source-schedule repair The historical v0.7 simulator does not recompute Ω\\Omega on every integration step. Its source loop is: if step≡0(mod10),Ω←Ωfast(a) \\boxed{ \\text{if step}\\equiv0\\pmod{10}, \\quad \\Omega\\leftarrow\\Omega_{\\mathrm fast}(a) } and otherwise holds the most recently computed Ω\\Omega. By contrast, Φ \\Phi is recomputed on every source step from the current and previous triangle amplitudes. An earlier autonomous-Φ\\Phi experiment in this research lineage updated Ω\\Omega every step. That execution therefore did not preserve the historical source schedule. Its conclusion that the Gaussian-Hartree second-moment dynamics necessarily suffers severe late-time autonomous drift is superseded. AUTO_FREEZE PRIOR CONCLUSION FULL_SECOND_MOMENT_AUTONOMY_FAILS_LATE is frozen as a source-schedule execution artifact. The prior file remains in provenance; its conclusion is not silently deleted. 2. Corrected autonomous Gaussian closure The repaired autonomous system uses: exact six-moment Gaussian Φ\\Phi functional; exact moment expression for Ω\\Omega; historical cadence Ω updated every 10 steps; \\Omega\\text{ updated every 10 steps}; historical velocity-Verlet propagation; Gaussian-Hartree cubic self-energy 3δ(μ2+C0). 3\\delta(\\mu^2+C_0). For seed 42, across the declared diagnostic checkpoints, mean relative discrepancies are: ϵμmean≈0.00519 \\boxed{ \\epsilon_\\mu^{\\mathrm mean}\\approx0.00519 } ϵC0mean≈0.00797 \\boxed{ \\epsilon_{C_0}^{\\mathrm mean}\\approx0.00797 } ϵΦmean≈0.00821 \\boxed{ \\epsilon_\\Phi^{\\mathrm mean}\\approx0.00821 } ϵΩmean≈0.00432. \\boxed{ \\epsilon_\\Omega^{\\mathrm mean}\\approx0.00432. } Maximum selected errors remain approximately: 2.50%for μ,3.79%for C0,3.47%for Φ,1.21%for Ω. 2.50\\%\\ \\text{for }\\mu, \\quad 3.79\\%\\ \\text{for }C_0, \\quad 3.47\\%\\ \\text{for }\\Phi, \\quad 1.21\\%\\ \\text{for }\\Omega. At step 219 the repaired Gaussian autonomous system gives: μG=0.00502655,μsrc=0.00504307, \\mu_{\\mathrm G}=0.00502655, \\qquad \\mu_{\\mathrm src}=0.00504307, C0,G=4.10955×10−6,C0,src=4.27132×10−6, C_{0,\\mathrm G}=4.10955\\times10^{-6}, \\qquad C_{0,\\mathrm src}=4.27132\\times10^{-6}, ΦG=0.889714,Φsrc=0.882488, \\Phi_{\\mathrm G}=0.889714, \\qquad \\Phi_{\\mathrm src}=0.882488, ΩG=0.864124,Ωsrc=0.861291. \\Omega_{\\mathrm G}=0.864124, \\qquad \\Omega_{\\mathrm src}=0.861291. Thus the severe late drift disappears after source-schedule repair. 3. Fresh candidat